window.GLOWSIS_2A = [{"id": 1, "title": "It's raining a lot", "en": "비가 너무 많이 오네요", "theme": "weather", "sections": [{"cls": "unit-flag", "html": "<div class=\"unit-flag\">UNIT 1 · WEATHER</div>"}, {"cls": "sec-title", "html": "<div class=\"sec-title\"><div class=\"no\">1</div><div><h2>It's raining a lot</h2><div class=\"en\">비가 너무 많이 오네요 — Weather · -네요 \"oh…!\" + 너무/아주/조금 + -고 있네요</div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "story", "html": "<div class=\"story\">\n    <img class=\"story-art\" src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n    <div class=\"story-body\">\n      <span class=\"story-tag\">💿 GLOWSIS STORY · NEW SEASON · WEATHER</span>\n      <h3>비 오는 날의 팬미팅 — \"비가 너무 많이 오네요!\"</h3>\n      <p>오늘은 <b>샛별</b>의 팬미팅 날이에요. 그런데 하늘을 보세요! 갑자기 <b>비</b>가 너무 많이 와요. 멤버들은 놀라서 말해요. \"우와, 비가 너무 많이 오네요! 그래도 <b>팬</b>들이 기다리고 있어요. 우리 힘내요!\" 💙</p>\n      <p class=\"story-en\">Today is <b>SAETBYEOL</b>'s fan-meeting day. But look at the sky — suddenly it starts to <b>rain</b> a lot! The members exclaim in surprise. \"Wow, it's raining so much! But our <b>fans</b> are waiting. Let's stay strong!\" 💙</p>\n      <span class=\"story-piece\">✨ NEW POINT · Notice the weather &amp; react with -네요!</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "goals", "html": "<div class=\"goals\">\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🌍</span> Talk about the weather &amp; react with surprise</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">👌</span> -네요 (oh…!) · 너무/아주/조금 (how much) · -고 있네요</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">⛅️</span> Weather vocabulary: rain, snow, wind, clouds &amp; more</div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "dialog", "html": "<div class=\"dialog\">\n    <div class=\"d-head\">\n      <span class=\"d-title\">💬 Dialogue 1 — It's Raining!</span>\n      <span class=\"d-scene\">🎦 In front of the fan-meeting venue</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">지우</div><div class=\"ko\">우리 팬미팅 날이에요! 그런데 하늘을 보세요. 비가 너무 많이 오네요!</div><div class=\"gl\">It's our fan-meeting day! But look at the sky. It's raining really a lot!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-05.webp\" alt=\"유나\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">유나</div><div class=\"ko\">맞아요, 지금 비가 오고 있네요. 우산을 안 가져왔어요… 😭</div><div class=\"gl\">You're right, it's raining right now. I didn't bring an umbrella… 😭</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/m-01.webp\" alt=\"지훈\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">지훈</div><div class=\"ko\">걱정하지 마요. 오늘은 바람이 아주 시원해요. 우리 조금 기다려요!</div><div class=\"gl\">Don't worry. The wind is very cool today. Let's wait a little!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-02.webp\" alt=\"서연\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">서연</div><div class=\"ko\">구름이 많네요. 그런데 팬들이 다 왔어요? 눈이 오면 어떡해요! 😂</div><div class=\"gl\">Oh, there are a lot of clouds. But have all the fans come? What if it snows! 😂</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/m-05.webp\" alt=\"하준\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">하준</div><div class=\"ko\">비가 와도 우리는 춤출 거예요! 팬들을 위해서요. 힘내요, 샛별! 💙</div><div class=\"gl\">Even if it rains, we'll dance! For our fans. Let's go, SAETBYEOL! 💙</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 1</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-네요 — \"Oh, I just noticed…!\" (realization &amp; exclamation)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Attach <b>-네요</b> to a verb or adjective stem to exclaim something you see or realize right now. 비가 오다 (rain \"comes\") → <b>비가 오네요!</b> \"Oh, it's raining!\" 덥다 (hot) → <b>덥네요!</b> \"Oh, it's hot!\" It sounds surprised but polite — perfect for noticing the weather.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">비가 오네요!</span><span class=\"gl\">Oh, it's raining! (오다 + -네요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">덥네요!</span><span class=\"gl\">Oh, it's hot! (덥다 → 덥네요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">날씨가 좋네요!</span><span class=\"gl\">Oh, the weather is nice!</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 2</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">너무 / 아주 / 조금 — \"too much / very / a little\" (degree words)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Put a degree word before an adjective or verb to say <b>how much</b>: <b>너무</b> = too / really, <b>아주</b> = very (a touch softer than 너무), <b>조금</b> = a little. 비가 <b>너무 많이</b> 와요 = rains too much, <b>아주</b> 추워요 = very cold, <b>조금</b> 더워요 = a little hot.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">비가 너무 많이 와요.</span><span class=\"gl\">It rains too much. (너무 + 많이)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">오늘 날씨가 아주 추워요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Today the weather is very cold.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">저는 조금 더워요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I'm a little hot. (조금 = a little)</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 3</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-고 있네요 — \"it's …ing!\" (ongoing action + realization)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Combine the progressive <b>-고 있어요</b> (…is …ing) with <b>-네요</b>. Result <b>-고 있네요</b> = you realize something is happening <b>right now</b>. 비가 오고 있어요 → <b>비가 오고 있네요</b> \"Oh, it's raining (right now)!\" 눈이 오고 있어요 → <b>눈이 오고 있네요</b> \"Oh, it's snowing!\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">비가 오고 있네요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Oh, it's raining right now! (오고 있네요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">눈이 오고 있네요!</span><span class=\"gl\">Oh, it's snowing! (눈 + 오고 있네요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">팬들이 노래하고 있네요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Oh, the fans are singing! (노래하다 → 노래하고 있네요)</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "teach", "html": "<div class=\"teach\">\n  <span class=\"t-label\">🧑‍🏫 Teacher's Deep-Dive · Breaking down \"비가 너무 많이 오네요\"</span>\n  <div class=\"t-q\"><span class=\"t-ko\">비가 너무 많이 오네요.</span> <span class=\"t-en\">= \"Oh, it's raining so much!\" (a soft exclamation)</span></div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-row t-head\">\n    <div class=\"t-why\">How do idols notice the weather and blurt it out mid-conversation? They stick a tiny surprise ending, <b>-네요</b>, onto the verb — and Koreans say rain &amp; snow \"come\" (오다) instead of \"fall\".</div>\n    <div class=\"t-deep\">\n      <b>-네요</b> is how you share a thought you <b>just noticed</b> — like stepping outside and seeing rain: <span class=\"pt-ko\">비가 오네요!</span> \"Oh, it's raining!\" Add a degree word in front to say how much: <b>너무</b> = \"too much / really\", <b>아주</b> = \"very\", <b>조금</b> = \"a little\". Put them together and you get\n      <span class=\"pt-ko\">비가 너무 많이 오네요</span> = \"Oh, it's raining really a lot!\"\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-grid\">\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">비가</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">rain <span class=\"t-sub\">(subject)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">비 = rain. The marker <b>가</b> shows rain is the thing doing the action. 눈 (snow), 바람 (wind), 구름 (cloud) work the same way.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">너무 많이</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">really a lot <span class=\"t-sub\">(degree + amount)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\"><b>너무</b> = too / really, <b>많이</b> = a lot (adverb form of 많다 \"many\"). So \"so much / a whole lot\".</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-eqcell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">오네요</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">it comes → \"oh, it's …ing!\" <span class=\"t-sub\">(오다 + -네요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">For weather Koreans say rain/snow \"come\": 오다. Add <b>-네요</b> for a surprised, polite \"oh…!\". For right-now action use <b>-고 있네요</b>: 비가 오고 있네요.</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-insight\">\n    <b class=\"t-i-ko\">-네요 = \"oh, I just noticed…!\"</b> — attach it to a verb or adjective stem to exclaim something you see or realize at this moment:\n    <span class=\"pt-ko\">비가 오네요!</span> (it's raining!), <span class=\"pt-ko\">덥네요!</span> (it's hot!), <span class=\"pt-ko\">춥네요!</span> (it's cold!). It sounds warm and a little surprised — idols say this a lot looking at the sky before a show.\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-compare\">\n    <div class=\"t-c-a\"><b>-어요 → plain statement</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">비가 와요.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">\"It rains.\" — just a fact, no surprise.</span></div>\n    <div class=\"t-c-b\"><b>-네요 → \"oh…!\" (just noticed)</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">비가 오네요!</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">\"Oh, it's raining!\" — you see it now and react.</span></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-tip\">\n    💡 <b>Memory tip:</b> degree words sit before the \"how\": <b>너무</b> (too much) · <b>아주</b> (very) · <b>조금</b> (a little). Look out the window and practice: <span class=\"pt-ko\">비가 너무 많이 오네요!</span> or on a nice day <span class=\"pt-ko\">하늘이 아주 맑네요!</span>\n  </div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "vocab-lab", "html": "<div class=\"vocab-lab\"><div class=\"vl-toolbar\"><span class=\"vl-hint\">카테고리를 눈러 그림과 함께 공부하세요</span><button class=\"vl-expand\" onclick=\"glowVocabAll()\">모두 펼치기</button></div><div class=\"vl-cat open\" data-tone=\"sky\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🌞</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">하늘과 날씨<small>Sky &amp; weather · 오늘 날씨가 어때요?</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">3</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a1_weather.webp\" alt=\"날씨\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('날씨')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">날씨</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">nalssi</div><div class=\"vw-en\">weather</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a1_sunny.webp\" alt=\"맑다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('맑다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">맑다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">makda</div><div class=\"vw-en\">clear / sunny</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a1_wind.webp\" alt=\"바람\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('바람')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">바람</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">baram</div><div class=\"vw-en\">wind</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('오늘 날씨가 어때요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">오늘 날씨가 어때요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">How is the weather today?</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('하늘이 아주 맑네요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">하늘이 아주 맑네요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Oh, the sky is so clear.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('바람이 많이 불어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">바람이 많이 불어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">It's very windy.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🌞 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 날씨(noun) takes the subject <b>이/가</b>: 날씨<b>가</b> 좋아요. 맑다 is an adjective \"clear\". 바람이 불어요 = \"wind blows\".</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"mint\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">☁</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">구름과 비·눈<small>Clouds, rain &amp; snow · 와요!</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">3</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a1_cloud.webp\" alt=\"구름\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('구름')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">구름</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">gureum</div><div class=\"vw-en\">cloud</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a1_rain.webp\" alt=\"비\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('비')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">비</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">bi</div><div class=\"vw-en\">rain</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b11_snow.webp\" alt=\"눈\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('눈')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">눈</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">nun</div><div class=\"vw-en\">snow</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('구름이 많아요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">구름이 많아요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">There are a lot of clouds.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('비가 너무 많이 오네요!')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">비가 너무 많이 오네요!</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Oh, it's raining really a lot!</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('눈이 오고 있네요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">눈이 오고 있네요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Oh, it's snowing right now.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">☁ <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 비<b>가</b> 와요 (rain \"comes\"), 눈<b>이</b> 와요 (snow \"comes\"), 구름<b>이</b> 많아요. Add <b>-고 있네요</b> to show it's happening right now: 오고 있네요!</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"pink\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🌡️</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">날씨 느낌<small>Temperature &amp; feelings · 더워요, 추워요</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">2</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a1_hot.webp\" alt=\"덥다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('덥다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">덥다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">deopda</div><div class=\"vw-en\">hot</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a1_cold.webp\" alt=\"춥다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('춥다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">춥다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">chupda</div><div class=\"vw-en\">cold</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('오늘은 너무 더워요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">오늘은 너무 더워요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">It's really hot today.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('겨울에는 날씨가 추워요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">겨울에는 날씨가 추워요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">In winter the weather is cold.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저는 조금 추워요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">저는 조금 추워요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I'm a little cold.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🌡️ <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 덥다 (hot) &amp; 춥다 (cold) are adjectives for how <i>you feel</i> and the weather. Degree word + them: 너무 더워요, 아주 추워요, 조금 더워요.</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[1-1] Reading — 비가 오네요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">지우: 비가 오네요.</span> What does Jiwoo say?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a1q1\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a1q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> It's raining!<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a1q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> It rained yesterday.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a1q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> I like the rain.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a1q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> It will rain tomorrow.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a1q1\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The ending <b class=\"hl\">-네요</b> adds surprise — you just noticed it. <b class=\"hl\">비가 오네요</b> = 비(rain) + 오다(come) + -네요 = <b class=\"hl\">\"Oh, it's raining!\"</b> It is not about the past, likes, or the future — it's happening now and you're reacting. ✨ Rule: verb stem + <b class=\"hl\">-네요</b> = \"oh…!\".</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[1-2] Reading — 비가 오고 있네요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">유나: 밖에 비가 오고 있네요.</span> What is Yuna saying?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a1q2\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a1q2',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> It rained this morning.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a1q2',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> It will rain tonight.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a1q2',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> It's raining right now — oh!<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a1q2',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> I don't like rain.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a1q2\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">-고 있네요</b> = <b class=\"hl\">-고 있어요</b> (…is happening now) + <b class=\"hl\">-네요</b> (just noticed). So <b class=\"hl\">오고 있네요</b> = \"Oh, it's coming right now!\" (it's raining as we speak). Not the past, not the future, not an opinion.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[1-3] Reading — 춥네요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose what Hajun just realized.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">하준: 오늘은 날씨가 춥네요!</span> Hajun says it is…</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a1q3\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a1q3',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> plainly cold (a fact, no surprise)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a1q3',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> going to be cold<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a1q3',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> cold before<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a1q3',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> cold — oh, I just noticed!<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a1q3\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">춥네요</b> = 춥다 (cold) + <b class=\"hl\">-네요</b>. The -네요 tells you he <b class=\"hl\">just noticed</b> and is exclaiming — \"Oh, it's cold!\" The plain form would be <span class=\"pt-ko\">추워요</span>, the future <span class=\"pt-ko\">춥겠어요</span>, the past <span class=\"pt-ko\">추웠어요</span>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[1-4] Grammar — 조금 (a little)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the degree word that means \"a little\".</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">서연: 저는 아직 괜찮아요. ______ 더워요.</span> It's only a LITTLE hot, not a lot. Fill in the best word.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a1q4\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a1q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 너무<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a1q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 조금<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a1q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 아주<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a1q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 많이<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a1q4\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">조금</b> = \"a little\". It sits before the adjective: <b class=\"hl\">조금 더워요</b> = \"I'm a little hot.\" <b>너무</b> = too much, <b>아주</b> = very, <b>많이</b> = a lot (used with verbs/amounts). Only 조금 fits \"a little\".</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[1-5] Grammar — 아주 (very)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct Korean sentence.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Translate \"Today the weather is very cold.\" using <span class=\"pt-ko\">아주</span>.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a1q5\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a1q5',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 오늘 날씨가 조금 추워요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a1q5',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 오늘 비가 너무 많이 와요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a1q5',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 오늘 날씨가 아주 추워요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a1q5',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 오늘 날씨가 좋아요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a1q5\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The target: \"very cold\" = <b class=\"hl\">아주 추워요</b>. Sentence <b>③</b> = 날씨(weather) + <b>아주</b>(very) + <b>추워요</b>(cold) — perfect. ① says \"a little cold\" (조금), ② is about rain (너무), ④ is \"nice weather\" with no degree word.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[1-6] Reading — 하늘이 맑아요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">지훈: 오늘 하늘이 맑아요.</span> Jihoon says…</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a1q6\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a1q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> The sky is clear / sunny.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a1q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> It is snowing.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a1q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> It is very windy.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a1q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> The sky is full of clouds.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a1q6\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">맑다</b> is an adjective meaning \"clear / sunny\". <b class=\"hl\">하늘이 맑아요</b> = \"the sky is clear.\" Snow is 눈이 와요, wind is 바람이 불어요, and clouds are 구름이 많아요 — none of those match.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[1-7] Reading — 구름과 비</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">유나: 구름이 많아요. 비가 오고 있네요!</span> What is Yuna saying?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a1q7\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a1q7',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> It's sunny but cold.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a1q7',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> It's cloudy — and oh, it's raining!<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a1q7',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> It snowed a little.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a1q7',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> I brought an umbrella.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a1q7\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">First <b class=\"hl\">구름이 많아요</b> = \"there are a lot of clouds\" (cloudy). Then <b class=\"hl\">비가 오고 있네요</b> = \"oh, it's raining right now!\" Cloudy weather + rain = ②.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[1-8] Grammar — 너무 많이</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct word.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">하준: 비가 ______ 와요. 정말 많이 와요!</span> Which word means \"too much\"?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a1q8\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a1q8',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 조금<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a1q8',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 많이<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a1q8',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 아주<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a1q8',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 너무<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a1q8\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">For \"too much / really a lot\" Koreans say <b class=\"hl\">너무 많이</b> — <b>너무</b> = too/really, <b>많이</b> = a lot. So <b class=\"hl\">비가 너무 많이 와요</b> = \"It rains too much.\" 조금 = a little (opposite!), 많이 alone = a lot, 아주 = very (no \"amount\" sense here).</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[1-9] Grammar — make -네요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct form.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">You want to exclaim to your friend: <span class=\"pt-ko\">눈이 와요</span> is plain. Add -네요 to sound surprised.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a1q9\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a1q9',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 눈이 와요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a1q9',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 눈이 왔어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a1q9',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 눈이 오네요!<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a1q9',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 눈이 올게요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a1q9\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Add <b class=\"hl\">-네요</b> to the verb stem 오다 → 오 + 네요 = <b class=\"hl\">오네요</b>. So \"Oh, it's snowing!\" = <b class=\"hl\">눈이 오네요!</b>. ① is plain (no surprise), ② is past, ④ means \"I'll come\" — not snow.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[1-10] Reading — 팬들이 노래해요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">서연: 우와, 팬들이 노래하고 있네요! 그리고 오늘 날씨가 너무 좋아요!</span> What does Seoyeon say?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a1q10\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a1q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> The fans are singing right now — and the weather is really nice!<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a1q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> The fans will sing tomorrow.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a1q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> It's raining so I'm sad.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a1q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> The fans are eating and it's cold.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a1q10\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Combine the pieces: <b class=\"hl\">팬들이 노래하고 있네요</b> = \"the fans are singing right now (oh!)\" and <b class=\"hl\">날씨가 너무 좋아요</b> = \"the weather is really nice.\" Both parts match only ①.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "culture", "html": "<div class=\"culture\">\n    <span class=\"c-label\">🎤 K-POP TIP</span>\n    <h3>Weather Talk Before the Fan Meeting!</h3>\n    <p>Before a show, idols peek at the sky and exclaim — that's the perfect moment to use -네요. Whether it's a sunny day or pouring rain, Koreans love to talk about the weather to start a friendly conversation.</p>\n    <div class=\"c-tip\">✍️ Look out the window and try: \"오늘 날씨가 정말 좋네요! \" (Today the weather is really nice!) or \"비가 너무 많이 오네요. 우산을 가져오세요!\" (It's raining so much. Bring an umbrella!) — you'll sound like an idol chatting backstage!</div>\n  </div>"}]}, {"id": 2, "title": "Go to Dongdaemun", "en": "동대문에 가 보세요", "theme": "shopping", "sections": [{"cls": "unit-flag", "html": "<div class=\"unit-flag\">UNIT 2 · SHOPPING</div>"}, {"cls": "sec-title", "html": "<div class=\"sec-title\"><div class=\"no\">2</div><div><h2>Go to Dongdaemun</h2><div class=\"en\">동대문에 가 보세요 — Shopping · -아/어 보세요 \"try doing\" + -아/어 보다 + -기 전에</div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "story", "html": "<div class=\"story\">\n    <img class=\"story-art\" src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n    <div class=\"story-body\">\n      <span class=\"story-tag\">💿 GLOWSIS STORY · NEW SEASON · SHOPPING</span>\n      <h3>동대문 쇼핑 대작전 — \"동대문에 가 보세요!\"</h3>\n      <p>오늘은 <b>샛별</b> 멤버들이 팬미팅에서 입을 옷과 <b>아이돌 굿즈</b>를 사러 갈 거예요! 리더 <b>지우</b>가 제안해요. \"동대문에 <b>가 보세요</b>! 옷하고 굿즈가 정말 많아요.\" 멤버들은 신나서 소리쳐요. \"그럼 <b>쇼핑하기 전에</b> 시장에도 가 볼게요!\" 💙</p>\n      <p class=\"story-en\">Today the <b>SAETBYEOL</b> members will go buy <b>idol merch</b> and clothes to wear at the fan meeting! Leader <b>Jiwoo</b> suggests, \"Try going to <b>Dongdaemun</b>! There are so many clothes and goods.\" The members cheer excitedly. \"Then <b>before we shop</b>, we'll also try the market!\" 💙</p>\n      <span class=\"story-piece\">✨ NEW POINT · Suggest a place with -아/어 보세요 &amp; time it with -기 전에!</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "goals", "html": "<div class=\"goals\">\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🌍</span> Suggest a place &amp; urge a friend to try it</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">👌</span> -아/어 보세요 (try doing!) · -아/어 보다 (give it a try) · -기 전에 (before)</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🛍️</span> Shopping &amp; transport vocab: Dongdaemun, market, clothes, bus, subway</div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "dialog", "html": "<div class=\"dialog\">\n    <div class=\"d-head\">\n      <span class=\"d-title\">💬 Dialogue 1 — The Merch Plan!</span>\n      <span class=\"d-scene\">🎦 At a shop near Dongdaemun</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">지우</div><div class=\"ko\">오늘은 팬미팅 굿즈를 사러 동대문에 가 볼까요?</div><div class=\"gl\">Should we try going to Dongdaemun today to buy fan-meeting merch?</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-05.webp\" alt=\"유나\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">유나</div><div class=\"ko\">네! 동대문에 가 보세요. 옷하고 굿즈가 정말 많아요!</div><div class=\"gl\">Yes! Try going to Dongdaemun. There are so many clothes and goods!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/m-01.webp\" alt=\"지훈\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">지훈</div><div class=\"ko\">좋아요! 그런데 쇼핑하기 전에 지하철 표부터 사요.</div><div class=\"gl\">Great! But before we shop, let's buy the subway ticket first.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-02.webp\" alt=\"서연\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">서연</div><div class=\"ko\">그리고 이 옷을 입어 보세요! 정말 예뻐요.</div><div class=\"gl\">And try on this shirt! It's really pretty.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/m-05.webp\" alt=\"하준\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">하준</div><div class=\"ko\">우와, 다 사고 싶어요! 근데 돈을 준비하기 전에 먼저 시장에 가 볼게요! 💙</div><div class=\"gl\">Wow, I want to buy everything! But before I prepare my money, I'll go try the market first! 💙</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 1</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-아/어 보세요 — \"Why don't you try…?\" (polite suggestion)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Attach <b>-아/어 보세요</b> to a verb stem to gently suggest someone <b>try</b> something. 가다 (go) → <b>가 보세요</b> \"try going\", 입다 (put on) → <b>입어 보세요</b> \"try it on\", 먹다 (eat) → <b>먹어 보세요</b> \"try eating\". The <b>보세요</b> part (from 보다 \"to see / try\") makes it a soft, friendly nudge — perfect for recommending a place or food.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">동대문에 가 보세요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Try going to Dongdaemun. (가다 + 아 보세요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">이 옷을 입어 보세요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Try on this shirt. (입다 → 입어 보세요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">이 음식을 먹어 보세요!</span><span class=\"gl\">Try this food! (먹다 → 먹어 보세요)</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 2</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-아/어 보다 — \"to try / to have the experience of doing\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Use <b>-아/어 보다</b> when you've actually <b>tried</b> or <b>experienced</b> something. 가다 → <b>가 봐요</b> \"I try going\", and in the past <b>가 봤어요</b> \"I tried / I've been (done it)\". This is the base of <b>가 보세요</b> — the -세요 just turns it into a polite suggestion.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">어제 동대문에 가 봤어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Yesterday I tried going to Dongdaemun. (가 보다 past)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">이 케이크를 먹어 봤어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I've tried this cake. (먹어 보다)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">지하철을 타 봤어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I've tried taking the subway. (타다 → 타 봤어요)</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 3</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-기 전에 — \"before doing…\" (timing)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Attach <b>-기 전에</b> to a verb stem to say <b>\"before [verb]\"</b>. The action that comes <b>before</b> 전에 happens <b>first</b>. 쇼핑하다 (shop) → <b>쇼핑하기 전에</b> \"before shopping\", 타다 (ride) → <b>타기 전에</b> \"before riding\".</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">쇼핑하기 전에 시장에 가요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I go to the market before shopping. (쇼핑하기 전에)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">지하철을 타기 전에 표를 사요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I buy a ticket before taking the subway. (타기 전에)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">밥을 먹기 전에 손을 씻어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I wash my hands before eating. (먹기 전에)</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "teach", "html": "<div class=\"teach\">\n  <span class=\"t-label\">🧑🏫 Teacher's Deep-Dive · Breaking down \"동대문에 가 보세요\"</span>\n  <div class=\"t-q\"><span class=\"t-ko\">동대문에 가 보세요.</span> <span class=\"t-en\">= \"Why don't you try going to Dongdaemun?\"</span></div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-row t-head\">\n    <div class=\"t-why\">How do you <b>suggest a place to an idol fan</b> or ask someone to <b>try</b> something? Two friendly endings: <b>-아/어 보세요</b> and <b>-기 전에</b>.</div>\n    <div class=\"t-deep\">\n      Today's unit is about <b>going, shopping, and timing</b>. <b>-아/어 보세요</b> means \"try doing (why don't you?)\" — the easy way to suggest a place, food, or experience.\n      <span class=\"pt-ko\">가 보세요</span> = \"try going!\", <span class=\"pt-ko\">입어 보세요</span> = \"try it on!\" And <b>-기 전에</b> answers <i>when</i>: <span class=\"pt-ko\">쇼핑하기 전에</span> = \"before shopping\".\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-grid\">\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">동대문에</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">to Dongdaemun <span class=\"t-sub\">(destination)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\"><b>에</b> marks the place you go to. 동대문 is a famous Seoul market district for clothes &amp; fabrics.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">가 보세요</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">try going <span class=\"t-sub\">(가다 + 아 보세요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\"><b>가다</b> → <b>가</b>, then add <b>-아 보세요</b> = \"try going!\". The 보세요 part makes it a polite suggestion.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-eqcell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">-기 전에</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">before (doing) <span class=\"t-sub\">(timing)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">Stick <b>-기 전에</b> on a verb to say \"before …\". 쇼핑<b>하기 전에</b> = \"before shopping\".</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-insight\">\n    <b class=\"t-i-ko\">-아/어 보세요 = \"try doing (please)\"</b> — a gentle suggestion. <b>가 보세요</b> \"try going\", <b>입어 보세요</b> \"try it on\", <b>먹어 보세요</b> \"try eating it\". It's how Koreans urge you to try a place or food without being pushy.\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-compare\">\n    <div class=\"t-c-a\"><b>-아/어 보세요 → try it (suggestion)</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">동대문에 가 보세요.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">\"Why don't you try going to Dongdaemun?\" — a gentle nudge.</span></div>\n    <div class=\"t-c-b\"><b>-기 전에 → before (timing)</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">쇼핑하기 전에 가 보세요.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">\"Try going before you shop.\" — marks the earlier action.</span></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-tip\">\n    💡 <b>K-pop memory trick:</b> Know a good spot? Use <span class=\"pt-ko\">-아/어 보세요</span> to <i>suggest</i> it, and <span class=\"pt-ko\">-기 전에</span> to talk about <i>when</i>. \"동대문에 <b>가 보세요</b>, 그리고 밥 먹<b>기 전에</b> 굿즈를 사세요!\" — \"Try Dongdaemun, and buy merch before you eat!\"\n  </div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "vocab-lab", "html": "<div class=\"vocab-lab\"><div class=\"vl-toolbar\"><span class=\"vl-hint\">카테고리를 눌러 그림과 함께 공부하세요</span><button class=\"vl-expand\" onclick=\"glowVocabAll()\">모두 펼치기</button></div><div class=\"vl-cat open\" data-tone=\"pink\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🛍️</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">어디로 갈까요?<small>Places to go · 가 보세요!</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">4</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a2_dongdaemun.webp\" alt=\"동대문\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('동대문')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">동대문</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">dongdaemun</div><div class=\"vw-en\">Dongdaemun (market area)</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u8_market.webp\" alt=\"시장\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('시장')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">시장</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">sijang</div><div class=\"vw-en\">market</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u8_shopping.webp\" alt=\"쇼핑\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('쇼핑')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">쇼핑</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">syoping</div><div class=\"vw-en\">shopping</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b12_tshirt.webp\" alt=\"옷\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('옷')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">옷</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">ot</div><div class=\"vw-en\">clothes</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('동대문에 가 보세요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">동대문에 가 보세요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Try going to Dongdaemun.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('쇼핑하기 전에 시장에 가요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">쇼핑하기 전에 시장에 가요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I go to the market before shopping.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('이 옷을 입어 보세요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">이 옷을 입어 보세요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Try on this shirt.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🛍️ <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> place + <b>에</b> + 가요/go, and <b>가 보세요</b> makes it a suggestion. 옷<b>을</b> 입다 (wear clothes), 쇼핑<b>을</b> 하다 (do shopping).</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"sky\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🚌</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">교통<small>Getting around · how to go</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">4</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a2_trygo.webp\" alt=\"가 보다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('가 보다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">가 보다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">ga boda</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to try going (go see)</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a2_trygo.webp\" alt=\"교통\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('교통')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">교통</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">gyotong</div><div class=\"vw-en\">transportation</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u7_bus.webp\" alt=\"버스\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('버스')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">버스</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">beoseu</div><div class=\"vw-en\">bus</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u7_subway.webp\" alt=\"지하철\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('지하철')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">지하철</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">jihacheol</div><div class=\"vw-en\">subway</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('지하철을 타기 전에 표를 사요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">지하철을 타기 전에 표를 사요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I buy a ticket before taking the subway.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('버스를 타고 동대문에 가요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">버스를 타고 동대문에 가요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I take a bus to Dongdaemun.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('동대문에 가 봤어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">동대문에 가 봤어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I've tried going to Dongdaemun.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🚌 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 교통 + 을/를 + 타요 (ride). 버스<b>를</b> 타요, 지하철<b>을</b> 타요. <b>-기 전에</b> marks when: 타기 전에 (before riding).</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[1] Reading — 동대문에 가 보세요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">지우: 동대문에 가 보세요.</span> What does Jiwoo suggest?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a2q1\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a2q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> Go to Dongdaemun. <i>(already going)</i><span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a2q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> Try going to Dongdaemun! (why don't you?)<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a2q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> I don&#39;t want to go to Dongdaemun.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a2q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> Dongdaemun is far away.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a2q1\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">-아/어 보세요</b> is a polite suggestion meaning <b class=\"hl\">\"try doing…\"</b>. <span class=\"pt-ko\">가다 → 가 보세요</span> = \"try going!\". So Jiwoo recommends giving Dongdaemun a try.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ The other options are about a fact, a wish not to go, or distance — none match a suggestion to \"try\".</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Rule: V + 아/어 보세요 = \"try V-ing (why don&#39;t you?)\" — perfect for recommending places and food.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[2] Reading — -기 전에 쇼핑</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">쇼핑하기 전에 시장에 가요.</span> When does the speaker go to the market?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a2q2\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a2q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> After shopping.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a2q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> Before shopping.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a2q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> While shopping.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a2q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> Never.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a2q2\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">-기 전에</b> means <b class=\"hl\">\"before doing…\"</b>. <span class=\"pt-ko\">쇼핑하다 → 쇼핑하기 전에</span> = \"before shopping\". So they visit the market first.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ \"After\" would use <span class=\"pt-ko\">-고 나서</span>, not 전에.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Rule: V + 기 전에 = \"before V-ing\". The action after 전에 is the first one.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[3] Reading — 옷을 입어 보세요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the sentence that means <i>\"Please try on the shirt.\"</i></div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Which one is a polite request to try something?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a2q3\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a2q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> <span class=\"pt-ko\">옷을 입어 보세요.</span><span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a2q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> <span class=\"pt-ko\">옷을 사요.</span><span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a2q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> <span class=\"pt-ko\">옷을 못 입어요.</span><span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a2q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> <span class=\"pt-ko\">옷을 입기 전에 사요.</span><span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a2q3\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">입다</span> (to wear/put on) → <span class=\"pt-ko\">입어 보세요</span> = <b class=\"hl\">\"try it on (please)\"</b>. A shop assistant says this when you can try clothes before buying.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">사요</b> = \"buy\", <b class=\"hl\">못 입어요</b> = \"can&#39;t wear\", and the last option adds \"before\", changing the meaning.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 입다 is a ㄷ-irregular verb → 입어요 / 입어 보세요.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[4] Reading — 고르기 전에 입어 보세요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">고르기 전에 직접 입어 보세요.</span> What should you do first?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a2q4\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a2q4',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> Try it on before you choose.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a2q4',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> Choose before you try it on.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a2q4',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> Don&#39;t choose any clothes.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a2q4',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> Buy it without looking.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a2q4\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Two rules together: <b class=\"hl\">-기 전에</b> (\"before\") and <b class=\"hl\">-아/어 보세요</b> (\"try doing\"). So: <b class=\"hl\">before choosing, try it on first</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ The order is flipped in option 2. Options 3 &amp; 4 add \"don&#39;t\" or \"without looking\" — not in the sentence.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 A shop assistant often says: \"고르기 전에 입어 보세요.\" = try before you buy!</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[5] Listening — what to do first</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Listen and choose what the speaker says to do FIRST.</div>\n\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('시장에 가기 전에 돈을 준비하세요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">What are you supposed to do first?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a2q5\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a2q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 서다 (stand)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a2q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 돈을 준비하다 (prepare money)<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a2q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 노래하다 (sing)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a2q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 운동하다 (exercise)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a2q5\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The audio says <span class=\"pt-ko\">시장에 가기 전에 돈을 준비하세요</span> — \"prepare money before going to the market\". <b class=\"hl\">-기 전에</b> marks the action that happens first.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ Going to the market is the later action; the others are distractors not mentioned.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Listen for <span class=\"pt-ko\">…기 전에</span> = the thing that happens before the -기 verb&apos;s action.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[6] Reading — -아/어 보세요 reply</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the best reply to the suggestion.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">가 보세요! 정말 재미있어요.</span> (Try going! It&#39;s really fun.)</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a2q6\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a2q6',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 네, 안 갈게요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a2q6',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 네, 꼭 한번 가 볼게요!<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a2q6',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 네, 저는 시장을 잘 몰라요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a2q6',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 네, 저 버스를 타요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a2q6\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">After a <b class=\"hl\">-아/어 보세요</b> suggestion, a natural reply is <span class=\"pt-ko\">꼭 한번 가 볼게요!</span> = <b class=\"hl\">\"I&#39;ll definitely give it a try!\"</b> — matching the \"try\" frame.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ The others reject the idea, ignore it, or answer a different question.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 한번 = \"once\", great with 보다 to say you&#39;ll give it a shot.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[7] Reading — find the NOT-correct sentence</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Which sentence is NOT correct?</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Pick the sentence that has a mistake.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a2q7\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a2q7',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> <span class=\"pt-ko\">지하철을 타기 전에 표를 사요.</span><span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a2q7',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> <span class=\"pt-ko\">이 옷을 맛보세요.</span><span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a2q7',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> <span class=\"pt-ko\">동대문에 가 보세요.</span><span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a2q7',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> <span class=\"pt-ko\">밥을 먹기 전에 손을 씻어요.</span><span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a2q7\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">You can&apos;t <b class=\"hl\">맛보다</b> (taste) clothes! <span class=\"pt-ko\">맛보세요</span> means \"please taste\", which doesn&apos;t fit 옷. It should be <span class=\"pt-ko\">입어 보세요</span>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ The others are all correct: 표를 사요 (buy a ticket) is natural, and 가 보세요 / 씻어요 are fine.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Check collocations: 옷 → 입다 (wear), 밥 → 먹다 (eat), 표 → 사다 (buy).</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[8] Listening — what did they try?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Listen and choose what the speaker DID (tried).</div>\n\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('어제 동대문에 가 봤어요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">What did the speaker try yesterday?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a2q8\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a2q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 동대문에 가 보다 (try going to Dongdaemun)<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a2q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 자전거를 타 보다 (try riding a bike)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a2q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 노래를 배워 보다 (try learning to sing)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a2q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 수영을 해 보다 (try swimming)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a2q8\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The audio says <span class=\"pt-ko\">어제 동대문에 가 봤어요</span> — <b class=\"hl\">\"yesterday I tried/experienced going to Dongdaemun\"</b>. <b>가 보다</b> in past tense = <span class=\"pt-ko\">가 봤어요</span>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ Biking, singing, and swimming are distractors from other activities.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <b>가다 → 가 봐요 → 가 봤어요</b>. Past 보다 = \"gave it a try (and did it)\".</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[9] Reading — where idols shop</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read the notice and choose the correct answer.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">아이돌 굿즈를 사기 전에 둘러보세요!</span> What should you do before buying idol merch?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a2q9\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a2q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> Look around first.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a2q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> Buy it immediately.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a2q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> Never buy anything.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a2q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> Sing to the staff.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a2q9\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">사기 전에 둘러보세요</span> = <b class=\"hl\">\"look around before buying\"</b>. <b>둘러보다</b> = \"look around / browse\". A handy tip for K-pop merch here!</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ \"Buy it immediately\" contradicts -기 전에. The others add actions not mentioned.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 굿즈 (merch) + 둘러보다 — real fans compare prices first!</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[10] Listening — the K-pop shopping plan</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Listen and choose the best summary.</div>\n\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('공연을 보기 전에 쇼핑을 할게요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">What is the speaker&#39;s plan?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a2q10\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a2q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> Shop before going to the concert.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a2q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> Go to the concert before shopping.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a2q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> She won&#39;t go at all.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a2q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> She only buys a ticket.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a2q10\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The audio says <span class=\"pt-ko\">공연을 보기 전에 쇼핑을 할게요</span> — <b class=\"hl\">\"I&#39;ll shop before watching the concert.\"</b> <span class=\"pt-ko\">-기 전에</span> = \"before\", so shopping happens first.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ Option 2 flips the order; the other two say she won&apos;t go or only buys a ticket — not in the audio.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Shop first, then enjoy the concert — a real fan&apos;s plan!</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "culture", "html": "<div class=\"culture\">\n    <span class=\"c-label\">🎤 K-POP TIP</span>\n    <h3>Dongdaemun — The K-Pop Fan's Shopping Spot!</h3>\n    <p>Dongdaemun is a famous Seoul market district packed with clothes, fabrics, and lots of K-pop goods. Fans love using -아/어 보세요 to recommend spots to each other — \"여기 가 보세요!\" (Try going here!).</p>\n    <div class=\"c-tip\">✍️ Next time you shop, try: \"이 굿즈를 사기 전에 가격을 비교해 보세요!\" (Before buying this merch, try comparing the price!) or \"동대문에 가 보세요!\" — you'll sound like a real fan guiding your friends!</div>\n  </div>"}]}, {"id": 3, "title": "What does mom's friend look like?", "en": "엄마 친구는 어떻게 생겼어요", "theme": "appearance", "sections": [{"cls": "unit-flag", "html": "<div class=\"unit-flag\">UNIT 3 · LOOKS &amp; APPEARANCE</div>"}, {"cls": "sec-title", "html": "<div class=\"sec-title\"><div class=\"no\">3</div><div><h2>What does mom's friend look like?</h2><div class=\"en\">엄마 친구는 어떻게 생겼어요? — Describing looks · 어떻게 생겼어요? + -는데</div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "story", "html": "<div class=\"story\">\n    <img class=\"story-art\" src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n    <div class=\"story-body\">\n      <span class=\"story-tag\">💿 GLOWSIS STORY · NEW SEASON · LOOKS</span>\n      <h3>멤버를 찾아 주세요 — \"어떻게 생겼어요?\"</h3>\n      <p>팬 사인회에 새 팬이 왔어요. 그런데 자기가 좋아하는 멤버를 못 찾아요! <b>지우</b>가 물어요. \"그 멤버는 <b>어떻게 생겼어요?</b>\" 팬이 대답해요. \"<b>키가 커요</b>. 그리고 <b>머리가 길어요</b>...\" 사인회장에서 사람들은 <b>외모</b>로 멤버를 찾아요. 엄마 친구를 찾는 것처럼요! 😄</p>\n      <p class=\"story-en\">A new fan arrives at a fan-signing — but can't find the member they like! <b>Jiwoo</b> asks, \"What does that member <b>look like</b>?\" The fan answers, \"<b>He's tall</b>. And <b>his hair is long</b>...\" Around the hall, fans find their idols by their <b>looks</b> — just like finding mom's friend! 😄</p>\n      <span class=\"story-piece\">✨ NEW POINT · Ask &amp; describe how someone looks!</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "goals", "html": "<div class=\"goals\">\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🗣️</span> Ask \"어떻게 생겼어요?\" about someone's looks</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">👀</span> Describe hair, face &amp; height (키/머리/눈…이/가 + adjective)</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🤓</span> Link ideas with -는데 (but / background)</div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "dialog", "html": "<div class=\"dialog\">\n    <div class=\"d-head\">\n      <span class=\"d-title\">💬 Dialogue 3 — Who is it?</span>\n      <span class=\"d-scene\">🎪 Idol fan-signing</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">지우</div><div class=\"ko\">안녕하세요! 오늘 누구를 만나고 싶어요?</div><div class=\"gl\">Hello! Who would you like to meet today?</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-05.webp\" alt=\"유나\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">유나</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 서연 언니를 찾아요. 서연 언니는 어떻게 생겼어요?</div><div class=\"gl\">I'm looking for Seoyeon unnie. What does she look like?</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">지우</div><div class=\"ko\">서연이는 눈이 커요. 그리고 머리가 길어요.</div><div class=\"gl\">Seoyeon has big eyes. And long hair.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-05.webp\" alt=\"유나\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">유나</div><div class=\"ko\">아! 저기 있는데 안경을 써요.</div><div class=\"gl\">Oh! She's over there, but she's wearing glasses.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">지우</div><div class=\"ko\">아니에요. 안경을 쓴 사람은 하준이예요! 하준이는 키가 작아요. 서연이는 키가 커요.</div><div class=\"gl\">No — the one with glasses is Hajun! Hajun is short. Seoyeon is tall.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-05.webp\" alt=\"유나\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">유나</div><div class=\"ko\">아, 맞아요! 이제 찾았어요. 😂 외모로 사람을 찾는 건 어려워요!</div><div class=\"gl\">Ah, right! Now I found her. 😂 Finding someone by looks is hard!</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 1</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">어떻게 생겼어요? — \"What does ___ look like?\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">To ask how someone looks, use <b>어떻게</b> (how) + the verb <b>생기다</b> (to be formed). So <b>어떻게 생겼어요?</b> literally asks \"how is he/she made?\" — i.e. <b>what do they look like?</b> Answer by describing: 키가 커요 (tall), 머리가 길어요 (long hair), 눈이 커요 (big eyes).</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">엄마 친구는 어떻게 생겼어요?</span><span class=\"gl\">How does mom's friend look?</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">그 가수는 어떻게 생겼어요?</span><span class=\"gl\">What does that singer look like?</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">지우 씨는 어떻게 생겼어요? 키가 커요.</span><span class=\"gl\">What does Jiwoo look like? She's tall.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 2</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">Describing looks — 키/머리/눈 + 이/가 + descriptive word</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Name a part with <b>이/가</b>, then a describing word (형용사) ending in <b>-아요/-어요</b>. 키가 커요 (is tall), 머리가 길어요 (hair is long), 눈이 커요 (eyes are big), 얼굴이 작아요 (face is small), 안경을 써요 (wears glasses). The describing word tells how the person looks.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">서연은 눈이 커요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Seoyeon has big eyes.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">하준이는 키가 작아요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Hajun is short. (키 = height)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">엄마는 머리가 길어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Mom's hair is long.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 3</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-는데 — \"but\" / giving a little background</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Add <b>-는데</b> (after a verb) or <b>-ㄴ데</b> (after most describing words ending in -아요/-어요) to say <b>\"but…\"</b> or to set the scene before your main point. 크다 → <b>큰데</b> (is tall but…), 작다 → <b>작은데</b>, 웃다 → <b>웃는데</b>. It makes Korean sound soft and connected.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">얼굴이 작은데 키가 커요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Her face is small, but she's tall.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">키가 큰데 머리가 짧아요.</span><span class=\"gl\">He's tall, but his hair is short.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">지금 저기 있는데 안경을 써요.</span><span class=\"gl\">She's over there now, and (note) she's wearing glasses.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "teach", "html": "<div class=\"teach\">\n  <span class=\"t-label\">🧑‍🏫 Teacher's Deep-Dive · Breaking down \"엄마 친구는 어떻게 생겼어요?\"</span>\n  <div class=\"t-q\"><span class=\"t-ko\">엄마 친구는 어떻게 생겼어요?</span> <span class=\"t-en\">= \"What does mom's friend look like?\"</span></div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-row t-head\">\n    <div class=\"t-why\">You're waiting to meet someone you've never seen — mom's friend, a new classmate, an idol at a fan-sign. How do you ask what they look like?</div>\n    <div class=\"t-deep\">\n      Ask with <b>어떻게</b> (how) + <b>생겼어요</b>. 생기다 means \"to be created / formed\", so how is that person <b>made</b>? To answer, point at a part (키, 머리, 눈, 얼굴) with <b>이/가</b> and give a describing word:\n      <span class=\"pt-ko\">키가 커요</span> = \"is tall\", <span class=\"pt-ko\">머리가 길어요</span> = \"hair is long\". Listen for whether the describing word is about <b>size/shape</b> (커요, 작아요, 길어요) or a <b>look</b> (예뻐요, 잘생겼어요).\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-grid\">\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">엄마 친구는</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">mom's friend <span class=\"t-sub\">(topic)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">엄마 + 친구 = \"mom's friend\". <b>는</b> marks the person we're asking about.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">어떻게</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">how <span class=\"t-sub\">(question word)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">You already know 어떻게 for \"how do you…\". Here it asks <b>how does she look?</b></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-eqcell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">생겼어요?</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">does look? <span class=\"t-sub\">(생기다 → 생겼어요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\"><b>생기다</b> (to be formed) → <b>생겼어요</b>. Together: \"How is she made / what does she look like?\"</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-insight\">\n    <b class=\"t-i-ko\">Answer with a part + 이/가 + describing word</b> — don't answer with a name or a \"feeling\". If someone asks 어떻게 생겼어요, describe: <b>키가 커요</b> (tall), <b>눈이 커요</b> (big eyes), <b>머리가 길어요</b> (long hair), <b>안경을 써요</b> (wears glasses).\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-compare\">\n    <div class=\"t-c-a\"><b>어떻게 생겼어요? → ask about looks</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">그 친구는 어떻게 생겼어요?</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">\"What does that friend look like?\" — the speaker has NOT seen them yet.</span></div>\n    <div class=\"t-c-b\"><b>Add -는데 to soften &amp; connect</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">키가 큰데 얼굴이 작아요.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">\"He's tall, but his face is small.\" — -는데 = \"but\" / background.</span></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-tip\">\n    💡 <b>Memory tip:</b> asking looks = <b>어떻게 + 생겼어요?</b> Answering looks = a <b>part</b> (키/머리/눈) + <b>이/가</b> + a <b>describing word</b>. Practice on a friend: <span class=\"pt-ko\">친구는 어떻게 생겼어요?</span> and answer <span class=\"pt-ko\">키가 커요, 눈이 커요!</span> Like a fan finding their idol! 😄\n  </div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "vocab-lab", "html": "<div class=\"vocab-lab\"><div class=\"vl-toolbar\"><span class=\"vl-hint\">카테고리를 눌러 그림과 함께 공부하세요</span><button class=\"vl-expand\" onclick=\"glowVocabAll()\">모두 펼치기</button></div><div class=\"vl-cat open\" data-tone=\"sky\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">👀</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">얼굴<small>Face · 눈·코·입</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">4</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a3_eye.webp\" alt=\"눈\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('눈')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">눈</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">nun</div><div class=\"vw-en\">eye</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a3_nose.webp\" alt=\"코\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('코')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">코</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">ko</div><div class=\"vw-en\">nose</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a3_mouth.webp\" alt=\"입\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('입')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">입</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">ip</div><div class=\"vw-en\">mouth</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a3_face.webp\" alt=\"얼굴\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('얼굴')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">얼굴</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">eolgul</div><div class=\"vw-en\">face</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('그 사람은 눈이 커요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">그 사람은 눈이 커요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">That person has big eyes.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('서연이는 얼굴이 작아요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">서연이는 얼굴이 작아요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Seoyeon has a small face.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('코가 높아요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">코가 높아요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">She has a high nose.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('입이 작아요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">입이 작아요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">He has a small mouth.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">👀 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> face part + 이/가 + describing word. 눈<b>이</b> 커요 (big eyes), 코<b>가</b> 높아요 (high nose), 얼굴<b>이</b> 작아요 (small face). 얼굴 = the whole face!</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"pink\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">💇</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">머리와 키<small>Hair &amp; height · 길어요·짧아요</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">2</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a3_hair.webp\" alt=\"머리\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('머리')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">머리</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">meori</div><div class=\"vw-en\">hair</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a3_height.webp\" alt=\"키\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('키')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">키</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">ki</div><div class=\"vw-en\">height</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('머리가 길어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">머리가 길어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">(The) hair is long.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('머리가 짧아요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">머리가 짧아요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">(The) hair is short.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('키가 커요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">키가 커요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">(He/She) is tall.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('키가 작아요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">키가 작아요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">(He/She) is short.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">💇 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 머리 = hair (길어요 = long / 짧아요 = short), 키 = height (커요 = tall / 작아요 = short). 멤버 머리<b>가</b> 길어요, 키<b>가</b> 커요!</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"lav\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">😊</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">안경과 웃음<small>Glasses &amp; smile · 안경을 써요</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">2</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a3_glasses.webp\" alt=\"안경\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('안경')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">안경</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">angyeong</div><div class=\"vw-en\">glasses</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a3_smile.webp\" alt=\"웃다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('웃다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">웃다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">utda</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to smile</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('안경을 써요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">안경을 써요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">(He/She) wears glasses.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('안경을 안 써요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">안경을 안 써요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">(He/She) doesn't wear glasses.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('웃으면 예뻐요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">웃으면 예뻐요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">(She's) pretty when she smiles.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('자꾸 웃어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">자꾸 웃어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">(He/She) keeps smiling.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">😊 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 안경<b>을</b> 써요 (wear glasses), 웃<b>으면</b> 예뻐요 (pretty when smiling). 안경을 쓴 멤버 = the member who wears glasses!</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[3-1] Reading — 어떻게 생겼어요?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct meaning.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">가: 그 친구는 어떻게 생겼어요?</span> What is the speaker asking?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a3q1\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a3q1',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> What is the friend's name?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a3q1',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> Where is the friend from?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a3q1',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> What does the friend look like?<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a3q1',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> How old is the friend?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n<div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a3q1\"></div><div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The question ends with <b class=\"hl\">어떻게 생겼어요?</b> — <b class=\"hl\">어떻게</b> (how) + <b>생겼어요</b> (is made / looks). It asks <b class=\"hl\">what the friend looks like</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ The other three are about a name, a hometown, and an age — none match a \"how does he look\" question.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Rule: <span class=\"pt-ko\">N은/는 어떻게 생겼어요?</span> = \"What does N look like?\"</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[3-2] Reading — 안경을 써요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct meaning.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">엄마 친구는 안경을 써요.</span> What does this mean?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a3q2\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a3q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> Mom's friend is tall.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a3q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> Mom's friend wears glasses.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a3q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> Mom's friend is pretty.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a3q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> Mom's friend has long hair.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n<div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a3q2\"></div><div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">안경을 써요</b> = <b class=\"hl\">wears glasses</b>. 쓰다 here means \"to put on / wear\" (as in glasses). The sentence says mom's friend <span class=\"pt-ko\">안경을 써요</span>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ Tall is <span class=\"pt-ko\">키가 커요</span>, pretty is <span class=\"pt-ko\">예뻐요</span>, long hair is <span class=\"pt-ko\">머리가 길어요</span> — none are in the sentence.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 안경<b class=\"hl\">을</b> 써요 — glasses is the object you \"wear\".</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[3-3] Reading — make the description</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct Korean.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">\"My mom's hair is long.\"</span> — choose the correct Korean.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a3q3\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a3q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 엄마 머리가 길어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a3q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 엄마 머리가 짧아요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a3q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 엄마 키가 커요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a3q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 엄마가 안경을 써요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n<div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a3q3\"></div><div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Hair = <b class=\"hl\">머리</b>, long = <b class=\"hl\">길어요</b>. \"My mom's hair is long\" = <span class=\"pt-ko\">엄마 머리가 길어요</span>. 엄마 says whose hair, 머리 names the part, 가 marks it, 길어요 describes it.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">짧아요</b> = short, <b class=\"hl\">키가 커요</b> = is tall, and 안경을 써요 = wears glasses — all change the meaning.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 길다 (long) → <span class=\"pt-ko\">길어요</span>.</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[3-4] Reading — 어떻게 (　)?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct ending.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">저 사람은 어떻게 (　)?</span> Choose the correct word to ask about looks.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a3q4\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a3q4',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 있어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a3q4',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 좋아해요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a3q4',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 먹어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a3q4',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 생겼어요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n  </div>\n<div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a3q4\"></div><div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">To ask \"how does that person look?\" you pair <b class=\"hl\">어떻게</b> with <b class=\"hl\">생기다</b>: <span class=\"pt-ko\">어떻게 생겼어요?</span> So the blank is <b class=\"hl\">생겼어요</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 있어요 (there is), 좋아해요 (likes), 먹어요 (eats) don't fit an appearance question.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 어떻게 + 생기다 = \"to be formed how\" → <span class=\"pt-ko\">어떻게 생겼어요?</span></div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[3-5] Reading — -는데 (but)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct meaning.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">민수 씨는 얼굴이 작은데 키가 커요.</span> What does this mean?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a3q5\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a3q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> Minsu has a small face but is tall.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a3q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> Minsu has a big face.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a3q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> Minsu is short.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a3q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> Minsu has long hair.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n<div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a3q5\"></div><div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">얼굴이 작은데</b> = \"face is small, BUT…\" — the ending <b class=\"hl\">-ㄴ데</b> adds a \"but\" that leads into the second half. Full meaning: <b class=\"hl\">small face, but tall</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 작아요 = small (not big), 커요 = tall (not short), and there is no hair word — the others are wrong.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 descriptive word -아요/-어요 + ㄴ데 = \"but…\": 작아요 → <span class=\"pt-ko\">작은데</span>, 커요 → <span class=\"pt-ko\">큰데</span>.</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[3-6] Reading — 웃으면 예뻐요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct meaning.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">유나는 웃으면 예뻐요.</span> What does this mean?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a3q6\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a3q6',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> Yuna is tall.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a3q6',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> Yuna wears glasses.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a3q6',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> Yuna is pretty when she smiles.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a3q6',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> Yuna has short hair.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n<div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a3q6\"></div><div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">웃으면</b> = \"when (she) smiles\", <b class=\"hl\">예뻐요</b> = \"is pretty\". Together: <b class=\"hl\">Yuna is pretty when she smiles</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ Tall is 키가 커요, glasses is 안경을 써요, short hair is 머리가 짧아요 — none match 웃으면 예뻐요.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 웃다 → <span class=\"pt-ko\">웃으면</span> (when/if you smile) + 예뻐요.</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[3-7] Listening — 지훈이를 찾아요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Listen and choose what is true about Jihoon.</div>\n  <button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('지훈 씨는 키가 커요. 머리는 짧아요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">What is true about Jihoon?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a3q7\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a3q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> He is tall with short hair.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a3q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> He is short with long hair.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a3q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> He is tall with long hair.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a3q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> He wears glasses.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n<div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a3q7\"></div><div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The audio: <span class=\"pt-ko\">지훈 씨는 키가 커요</span> (Jihoon is tall) and <span class=\"pt-ko\">머리는 짧아요</span> (his hair is short). So he is <b class=\"hl\">tall with short hair</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ The others mix up long/short hair or add glasses, which the audio never says.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Listen for 키<b class=\"hl\">가</b> 커요 (tall) and 머리<b class=\"hl\">가</b> 짧아요 (short hair).</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[3-8] Reading — 그 가수는 어떻게 생겼어요?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the best reply.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">그 가수는 어떻게 생겼어요?</span> Choose the best answer.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a3q8\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a3q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 머리가 길고 눈이 커요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a3q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 노래를 잘해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a3q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 서울에 살아요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a3q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 스무 살이에요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n<div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a3q8\"></div><div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The question asks <b class=\"hl\">what the singer looks like</b>, so the answer must describe appearance: <span class=\"pt-ko\">머리가 길고 눈이 커요</span> (long hair and big eyes).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ Singing well (노래를 잘해요), living in Seoul (서울에 살아요), and being 20 (스무 살이에요) describe ability, place, and age — not looks.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Answer 어떻게 생겼어요? with <span class=\"pt-ko\">키/머리/눈 …이/가 + describing word</span>.</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[3-9] Listening — 누가 안경을 써요?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Listen and choose who wears glasses.</div>\n  <button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('지우는 안경을 안 써요. 하준이는 안경을 써요. 그리고 키가 작아요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Listen to the audio. Who wears glasses?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a3q9\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a3q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 지우<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a3q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 하준<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a3q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 유나<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a3q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 서연<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n<div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a3q9\"></div><div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The audio: <span class=\"pt-ko\">지우는 안경을 안 써요</span> (Jiwoo does NOT wear glasses), but <span class=\"pt-ko\">하준이는 안경을 써요</span> (Hajun DOES). The wearer is <b class=\"hl\">하준</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 지우 has <b class=\"hl\">안</b> (not) before 써요 = \"doesn't wear\", so Jiwoo is wrong; the other two names aren't mentioned.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Listen for <span class=\"pt-ko\">안 써요</span> (doesn't wear) vs <span class=\"pt-ko\">써요</span> (wears).</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[3-10] Listening — 엄마 친구를 찾아요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Listen and choose the best description.</div>\n  <button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('엄마 친구는 머리가 길어요. 그리고 키가 커요. 안경도 써요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">What does mom's friend look like?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a3q10\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a3q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> Tall, with long hair and glasses.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a3q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> Short, with short hair.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a3q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> Long hair but no glasses.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a3q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> Young, with big eyes.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n<div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a3q10\"></div><div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The audio lists three looks: <b class=\"hl\">머리가 길어요</b> (long hair), <b class=\"hl\">키가 커요</b> (tall), and <b class=\"hl\">안경도 써요</b> (also wears glasses). Best summary = <b class=\"hl\">tall, with long hair and glasses</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ Short hair, \"no glasses\", and \"young with big eyes\" contradict or add to the audio.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Chain descriptions: 머리가 길고 키가 커요, 안경을 써요 — like spotting mom's friend across the room!</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "culture", "html": "<div class=\"culture\">\n    <span class=\"c-label\">🎤 K-POP TIP</span>\n    <h3>Spot Your Idol by Looks!</h3>\n    <p>Every fan has a way to find their bias in a crowd — \"the tall one\", \"the one with long hair\", \"the one who wears glasses\". Describing members by their looks is a daily K-pop skill. Ask 어떻게 생겼어요? and point out the features that make someone easy to spot!</p>\n    <div class=\"c-tip\">✍️ \"그 멤버는 어떻게 생겼어요? 키가 크고 머리가 길어요. 웃으면 예뻐요!\" — \"(What does that member look like? He/She is tall with long hair — and pretty when smiling!)\"</div>\n  </div>"}]}, {"id": 4, "title": "How about making bulgogi?", "en": "불고기를 해 먹는 게 어때요?", "theme": "suggestions", "sections": [{"cls": "unit-flag", "html": "<div class=\"unit-flag\">UNIT 4 · SUGGESTIONS</div>"}, {"cls": "sec-title", "html": "<div class=\"sec-title\"><div class=\"no\">4</div><div><h2>How about making bulgogi?</h2><div class=\"en\">불고기를 해 먹는 게 어때요? — Suggestions · -아/어 먹다 &amp; -는 게 어때요?</div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "story", "html": "<div class=\"story\">\n    <img class=\"story-art\" src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n    <div class=\"story-body\">\n      <span class=\"story-tag\">💿 GLOWSIS STORY · NEW SEASON · COOKING TOGETHER</span>\n      <h3>불고기를 해 먹는 게 어때요?</h3>\n      <p>연습이 끝난 뒤 멤버들이 <b>저녁</b>을 이야기해요. <b>지우</b>가 말해요. \"우리 <b>불고기</b>를 해 먹는 게 어때요? <b>김치</b>하고 <b>밥</b>도 준비해요!\" 다섯 명이 <b>함께</b> <b>요리</b>해서 재미있게 먹어요. 😋</p>\n      <p class=\"story-en\">After practice the members talk about <b>dinner</b>. <b>Jiwoo</b> suggests, \"How about making some <b>bulgogi</b>? Let's also prepare <b>kimchi</b> and <b>rice</b>!\" All five cook <b>together</b> and enjoy the meal. 😋</p>\n      <span class=\"story-piece\">✨ NEW POINT · Suggest doing something together!</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "goals", "html": "<div class=\"goals\">\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🗣️</span> Suggest doing something together</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🍳</span> -아/어 먹다 (make &amp; eat) vs -는 게 어때요? (how about)</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🍚</span> Food &amp; cooking vocabulary</div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "dialog", "html": "<div class=\"dialog\">\n    <div class=\"d-head\">\n      <span class=\"d-title\">💬 Dialogue 4 — Dinner Suggestion</span>\n      <span class=\"d-scene\">🍳 After practice at the dorm</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">지우</div><div class=\"ko\">다들 배고파요. 저녁에 뭘 해 먹을까요?</div><div class=\"gl\">Everyone is hungry. What shall we make and eat for dinner?</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-02.webp\" alt=\"서연\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">서연</div><div class=\"ko\">불고기를 해 먹는 게 어때요? 맛있고 쉽게 만들어요!</div><div class=\"gl\">How about making some bulgogi? It's tasty and easy to make!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/m-05.webp\" alt=\"하준\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">하준</div><div class=\"ko\">좋아요! 저는 김치하고 밥을 준비할까요?</div><div class=\"gl\">Great! Shall I prepare kimchi and rice?</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/m-01.webp\" alt=\"지훈\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">지훈</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 요리를 잘 못 해요. 같이 만들면 재미있을 거예요!</div><div class=\"gl\">I can't cook very well. It'll be fun if we make it together!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-05.webp\" alt=\"유나\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">유나</div><div class=\"ko\">좋아요! 우리 함께 만들어서 맛있게 먹어요!</div><div class=\"gl\">Okay! Let's make it together and eat well!</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 1</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-아/어 먹다 — \"make (it) and eat\" · do-and-eat</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">To say you <b>make/cook something and then eat it</b>, take a verb like <b>하다</b> (do) → <b>해</b>, then add <b>먹다</b> (eat): <b>해 먹다</b> = \"make and eat\". So <b>불고기를 해 먹어요</b> = \"I make (and eat) bulgogi\".</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">저녁에 불고기를 해 먹어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I make (and eat) bulgogi for dinner. (하다 → 해 먹다)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">우리는 함께 요리를 해 먹어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">We cook and eat together.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">서연은 밥을 만들어 먹어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Seoyeon makes rice and eats it. (만들다 → 만들어 먹다)</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 2</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-는 게 어때요? — \"How about …?\" (a suggestion)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">To suggest an idea softly, take a verb and add <b>-는 게 어때요?</b>. It turns the verb into \"doing …\" + \"how about?\": <b>해 먹는 게 어때요?</b> = \"How about making (and eating) it?\" This is a friendly, polite way to suggest.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">불고기를 해 먹는 게 어때요?</span><span class=\"gl\">How about making bulgogi?</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">같이 만들고 먹는 게 어때요?</span><span class=\"gl\">How about making and eating it together?</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">저녁에 김치를 먹는 게 어때요?</span><span class=\"gl\">How about eating kimchi for dinner?</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 3</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-(으)ㄹ까요? — \"Shall we …?\" (asking together)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">To ask someone \"shall we / should we do …?\", add <b>-ㄹ까요</b> after a vowel and <b>-을까요</b> after a final consonant. It invites the other person to do it with you: <b>뭘 해 먹을까요?</b> = \"What shall we make and eat?\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">우리 불고기를 만들어 먹을까요?</span><span class=\"gl\">Shall we make and eat bulgogi? (만들다 → 만들어, vowel → 을까요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">밥을 같이 먹을까요?</span><span class=\"gl\">Shall we eat together? (먹다 ends in ㄱ → 을까요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">오늘 저녁에 뭘 해 먹을까요?</span><span class=\"gl\">What shall we make and eat tonight?</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "teach", "html": "<div class=\"teach\">\n  <span class=\"t-label\">🧑‍🏫 Teacher's Deep-Dive · Breaking down \"불고기를 해 먹는 게 어때요?\"</span>\n  <div class=\"t-q\"><span class=\"t-ko\">불고기를 해 먹는 게 어때요?</span> <span class=\"t-en\">= \"How about making bulgogi?\"</span></div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-row t-head\">\n    <div class=\"t-why\">How does a Korean friend suggest cooking dinner together? It's not \"let's cook\" — it's two friendly endings that ask for your opinion.</div>\n    <div class=\"t-deep\">\n      Korean bundles two ideas into one verb: <b>해 먹다</b> literally joins <b>해</b> (from 하다, \"do/make\") + <b>먹다</b> (\"eat\") = \"make (it) and eat (it)\". Then <b>-는 게 어때요?</b> turns it into a gentle suggestion: <b>해 먹는 게 어때요?</b> = \"How about making (and eating) it?\" No pressure — you're just asking how it sounds.\n      To truly invite the person to join in, use <b>-(으)ㄹ까요?</b>: <span class=\"pt-ko\">뭘 해 먹을까요?</span> = \"What shall we make and eat?\"\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-grid\">\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">불고기를</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">bulgogi <span class=\"t-sub\">(object)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">불고기 is the tasty beef dish. <b>을</b> marks it as the thing being made and eaten.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">해 먹는</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">make-and-eat <span class=\"t-sub\">(해 + 먹다)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\"><b>해</b> (하다 → do/make) + <b>먹다</b> (eat) = \"make and eat\". Add <b>-는</b> to make it \"making-and-eating\".</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-eqcell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">게 어때요?</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">how about <span class=\"t-sub\">(suggestion)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\"><b>-는 게 어때요?</b> = \"how about …-ing?\" A soft, friendly way to suggest doing something.</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-insight\">\n    <b class=\"t-i-ko\">해 먹다 = \"make and eat\"</b> — one verb, two actions. <b>불고기를 해 먹는 게 어때요?</b> = \"How about making bulgogi?\" To invite your friend along, swap in <b>-을까요?</b>: <b>우리 함께 만들어 먹을까요?</b> = \"Shall we make and eat it together?\"\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-compare\">\n    <div class=\"t-c-a\"><b>-는 게 어때요? → how about …? (soft suggestion)</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">불고기를 해 먹는 게 어때요?</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">\"How about making bulgogi?\" — asking what the person thinks.</span></div>\n    <div class=\"t-c-b\"><b>-(으)ㄹ까요? → shall we …? (invite together)</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">우리 함께 만들어 먹을까요?</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">\"Shall we make and eat it together?\" — inviting the person to join in.</span></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-tip\">\n    💡 <b>Memory tip:</b> cooking with friends has two friendly endings. Suggest an idea with <b>-는 게 어때요?</b> (how about …?), and invite your friend to join with <b>-(으)ㄹ까요?</b> (shall we …?). Try it:\n    <span class=\"pt-ko\">같이 저녁을 먹는 게 어때요?</span> (\"How about having dinner together?\")\n  </div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "vocab-lab", "html": "<div class=\"vocab-lab\"><div class=\"vl-toolbar\"><span class=\"vl-hint\">카테고리를 눌러 그림과 함께 공부하세요</span><button class=\"vl-expand\" onclick=\"glowVocabAll()\">모두 펼치기</button></div><div class=\"vl-cat open\" data-tone=\"pink\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🥘</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">음식<small>Food &amp; meals · 뭘 먹어요?</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">3</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a4_bulgogi.webp\" alt=\"불고기\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('불고기')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">불고기</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">bulgogi</div><div class=\"vw-en\">bulgogi (beef BBQ)</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a4_kimchi.webp\" alt=\"김치\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('김치')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">김치</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">gimchi</div><div class=\"vw-en\">kimchi</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a4_rice.webp\" alt=\"밥\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('밥')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">밥</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">bap</div><div class=\"vw-en\">rice / a meal</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('불고기를 해 먹는 게 어때요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">불고기를 해 먹는 게 어때요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">How about making bulgogi?</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('김치하고 밥을 먹어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">김치하고 밥을 먹어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I eat kimchi and rice.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🥘 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 불고기<b>를</b>, 김치<b>를</b>, 밥<b>을</b> — food nouns take 을/를 as the object. 밥 = a meal too (\"밥을 먹어요\" = I eat a meal).</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"sky\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🍳</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">요리와 동작<small>Cooking &amp; actions · 무엇을 해요?</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">3</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b9_cook.webp\" alt=\"요리\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('요리')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">요리</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">yori</div><div class=\"vw-en\">cooking</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a4_make.webp\" alt=\"만들다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('만들다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">만들다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">mandeulda</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to make</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u5_eat.webp\" alt=\"먹다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('먹다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">먹다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">meokda</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to eat</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저는 요리를 잘 해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">저는 요리를 잘 해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I cook well.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('같이 불고기를 만들어 먹을까요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">같이 불고기를 만들어 먹을까요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Shall we make and eat bulgogi together?</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🍳 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 요리<b>를</b> 해요 (cook), 만들어 먹다 = make-and-eat. 만들다 → 만들어 (아), 먹다 → 먹어 (어).</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"lav\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🍽️</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">함께 저녁<small>Dinner together · 같이 먹어요</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">2</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b10_dinner.webp\" alt=\"저녁\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저녁')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">저녁</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">jeonyeok</div><div class=\"vw-en\">dinner / evening</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b10_together.webp\" alt=\"함께\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('함께')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">함께</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">hamkke</div><div class=\"vw-en\">together</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저녁에 무엇을 먹을까요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">저녁에 무엇을 먹을까요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">What shall we eat for dinner?</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('우리 함께 저녁을 먹는 게 어때요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">우리 함께 저녁을 먹는 게 어때요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">How about having dinner together?</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🍽️ <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 함께 is a lovely word for \"together\" (같이 is its spoken twin). <b>함께 만들어요</b> = let's make it together.</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[4-1] Reading — 불고기를 해 먹는 게 어때요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">지우: 저녁에 불고기를 해 먹는 게 어때요?</span> What does Jiwoo suggest?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a4q1\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a4q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> How about making bulgogi for dinner?<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a4q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> I ate bulgogi for dinner.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a4q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> Bulgogi is too expensive.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a4q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> Let's not cook tonight.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a4q1\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">-는 게 어때요?</b> at the end of a verb = a friendly <b class=\"hl\">\"how about …?\"</b> suggestion. <b>해 먹는</b> = \"making-and-eating\" (해 from 하다 + 먹다).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ The sentence asks HOW ABOUT making bulgogi — it does not say Jiwoo ate it, that it's expensive, or that they shouldn't cook.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Rule: suggest with <span class=\"pt-ko\">verb + 는 게 어때요?</span></div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[4-2] Reading — 무엇을 해 먹을까요?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">유나: 우리 오늘 저녁에 무엇을 해 먹을까요?</span> What is Yuna asking?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a4q2\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a4q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> What did we make for dinner yesterday?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a4q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> What shall we make and eat for dinner tonight?<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a4q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> Dinner is already on the table.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a4q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> Yuna will eat alone.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a4q2\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">-을까요?</b> = a soft <b class=\"hl\">\"shall we …?\"</b> that asks the listener to decide together. <b>해 먹을까요?</b> = \"shall we make-and-eat?\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ It is a future question about what to cook tonight (오늘 저녁), inviting the others — not the past, a statement, or eating alone.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Rule: invite together with <span class=\"pt-ko\">-(으)ㄹ까요?</span></div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[4-3] Reading — choose the correct form</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct polite ending.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">우리는 함께 불고기를 (　).</span> (We make-and-eat bulgogi together.)</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a4q3\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a4q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 해 먹어요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a4q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 해 먹어<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a4q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 해 먹었어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a4q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 해 먹을까요?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a4q3\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The sentence describes what \"we\" do regularly, so we need the friendly <b class=\"hl\">present tense</b>: 하다 → 해 + 먹다 = <b class=\"hl\">해 먹어요</b> = \"make and eat\".</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">해 먹어</b> is not polite, <b class=\"hl\">해 먹었어요</b> is the past, and <b class=\"hl\">해 먹을까요?</b> is a question.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 해 먹다 → 해 먹어요 (present polite).</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[4-4] Reading — which means \"how about\"?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Which sentence means \"How about …?\" (a suggestion)?</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Choose the sentence that suggests doing something.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a4q4\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a4q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 불고기를 해 먹어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a4q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 우리 같이 저녁을 먹어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a4q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 같이 불고기를 만들어 먹는 게 어때요?<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a4q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 저녁에 김치를 먹었어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a4q4\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">A suggestion uses <b class=\"hl\">-는 게 어때요?</b>. <b>만들어 먹는 게 어때요?</b> = \"how about making-and-eating it?\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ The first two are statements (\"we eat…\"), and the last is the past tense — none of them ask \"how about…?\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 -는 게 어때요? signals a friendly suggestion.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[4-5] Listening — what do they suggest?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Listen and choose what the speaker suggests.</div>\n\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('같이 불고기를 만들어 먹는 게 어때요?')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">What does the speaker suggest?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a4q5\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a4q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> eating alone<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a4q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> making and eating bulgogi together<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a4q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> going to a restaurant<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a4q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> eating breakfast<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a4q5\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The audio says <span class=\"pt-ko\">같이 불고기를 만들어 먹는 게 어때요?</span> = \"How about making and eating bulgogi together?\" — a suggestion.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ The key words are 함께/같이 (together) + 불고기 (bulgogi) + 해/만들어 먹다 (make-and-eat). Restaurants, breakfast, and eating alone are not mentioned.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Listen for <span class=\"pt-ko\">-는 게 어때요?</span> to spot a suggestion.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[4-6] Reading — 서연은 요리를 잘 해요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">서연: 저는 요리를 잘 해요. 그래서 불고기도 만들어 먹을 수 있어요.</span> What can Seoyeon do?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a4q6\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a4q6',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> She can't cook.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a4q6',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> She can cook well and can make bulgogi.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a4q6',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> She only eats out.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a4q6',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> She is too busy to cook.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a4q6\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">요리를 잘 해요</b> = \"cooks well\", and <b class=\"hl\">만들어 먹을 수 있어요</b> = \"can make-and-eat\" (만들다 + 먹다 + ㄹ 수 있어요 = ability).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ The sentence is positive about her cooking — not can't-cook, eat-out, or too-busy.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 만들어 먹다 + ㄹ 수 있어요 = \"can make-and-eat\".</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[4-7] Reading — choose the wrong sentence</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Which sentence is NOT correct?</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Pick the sentence that has a mistake.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a4q7\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a4q7',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 저녁에 김치를 먹어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a4q7',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 우리 함께 저녁을 먹는 게 어때요?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a4q7',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 저는 불고기를 좋아해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a4q7',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 저녁을 먹는 게 어때요를 해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a4q7\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">A suggestion already ends in <b class=\"hl\">-는 게 어때요?</b>, so you cannot add another verb after it. <b>어때요를 해요</b> stacks endings and is wrong.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ \"I eat kimchi for dinner\", \"how about having dinner together?\", and \"I like bulgogi\" are all correct, natural sentences.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <span class=\"pt-ko\">-는 게 어때요?</span> is already complete — don't attach 해요.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[4-8] Listening — who will make the rice?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Listen and choose what the person will prepare.</div>\n\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('저는 밥을 준비할게요. 김치는 하준이 만들어요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">What will this person prepare?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a4q8\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a4q8',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> kimchi<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a4q8',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> rice<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a4q8',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> bulgogi<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a4q8',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> nothing — they can't cook<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a4q8\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The audio says <span class=\"pt-ko\">저는 밥을 준비할게요. 김치는 하준이 만들어요.</span> = \"I'll prepare the rice. Hajun makes the kimchi.\" So this person will make <b class=\"hl\">rice</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ Kimchi belongs to Hajun, bulgogi is not mentioned, and the speaker can clearly help cook.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Listen for <span class=\"pt-ko\">준비할게요</span> (I'll prepare) + the food word.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[4-9] Reading — best reply</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the best reply to the question.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">우리 저녁에 불고기를 해 먹을까요?</span> (Shall we make bulgogi for dinner?)</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a4q9\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a4q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 네, 좋아요! 같이 만들어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a4q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 아니요, 지금 비가 와요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a4q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 저는 친구가 많아요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a4q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 불고기는 어제 먹을 거예요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a4q9\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">A <b class=\"hl\">-(으)ㄹ까요?</b> question (\"shall we …?\") wants an answer agreeing or declining. The natural reply is <b class=\"hl\">네, 좋아요! 같이 만들어요</b> = \"Yes, sounds good! Let's make it together.\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ The others talk about the weather, having friends, or a mixed-up time — they don't answer the suggestion.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Agree to a suggestion with <span class=\"pt-ko\">네, 좋아요!</span></div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[4-10] Listening — the dinner plan</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Listen and choose the best summary.</div>\n\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('우리 함께 불고기를 만들어 먹는 게 어때요? 네, 좋아요! 밥도 준비해요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">What do the speakers decide to do?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a4q10\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a4q10',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> They order food online.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a4q10',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> They make bulgogi and eat together for dinner.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a4q10',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> They go to sleep without dinner.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a4q10',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> Only one person cooks alone.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a4q10\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The dialogue: <span class=\"pt-ko\">우리 함께 불고기를 만들어 먹는 게 어때요? 네, 좋아요! 밥도 준비해요.</span> They agree to <b class=\"hl\">make bulgogi and eat together</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 함께/같이 (together) + 만들어 먹다 (make-and-eat) + a positive reply means they cook as a group — no delivery, no skipping dinner, no solo cooking.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Listen for 함께 + 해/만들어 먹다 + 좋아요 to catch the plan.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "culture", "html": "<div class=\"culture\">\n    <span class=\"c-label\">🎤 K-POP TIP</span>\n    <h3>Dinner Like a K-POP Group!</h3>\n    <p>K-pop idols practice all day, and after a long day nothing beats cooking and eating together. Idols often make a big shared meal — bulgogi, rice, and kimchi — and enjoy it as a team. Suggesting food is how groups bond!</p>\n    <div class=\"c-tip\">✍️ \"우리 ○○을 해 먹는 게 어때요? 네, 좋아요! 함께 만들어요!\" — \"(How about making (and eating) ○○? Yes, sounds good! Let's make it together!)\"</div>\n  </div>"}]}, {"id": 5, "title": "I'd like to order", "en": "주문할게요 — Ordering food at a restaurant · -을게요 · -을까요 · counting", "theme": "ordering", "sections": [{"cls": "unit-flag", "html": "<div class=\"unit-flag\">UNIT 5 · ORDERING</div>"}, {"cls": "sec-title", "html": "<div class=\"sec-title\"><div class=\"no\">5</div><div><h2>I'd like to order</h2><div class=\"en\">주문할게요 — Ordering food at a restaurant · -을게요 (I'll ~) · -을까요 (Shall I/we ~?) · counting 하나·두 개</div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "story", "html": "<div class=\"story\">\n    <img class=\"story-art\" src=\"assets/img/chars/f-02.webp\" alt=\"서연\">\n    <div class=\"story-body\">\n      <span class=\"story-tag\">💿 GLOWSIS STORY · NEW SEASON · ORDERING</span>\n      <h3>스케줄이 끝나면, 우리 뭐 먹을까요? — \"주문할게요!\"</h3>\n      <p>긴 스케줄이 끝나고 다섯 멤버가 <b>식당</b>에 가요. 모두 배가 고파요. \"<b>무엇을 먹을까요?</b>\" 서연이 <b>메뉴</b>를 보고 떡볶이를 골라요. \"<b>저는 매운 떡볶이를 주문할게요!</b>\" 멤버들은 하나씩 <b>주문</b>하고 맛있게 먹어요. 😋</p>\n      <p class=\"story-en\">After a long schedule the five members go to a <b>restaurant</b>. Everyone is hungry. \"What shall we <b>eat</b>?\" <b>Seoyeon</b> looks at the <b>menu</b> and picks tteokbokki. \"<b>I'll order</b> the spicy tteokbokki!\" Each member <b>orders</b> something and they eat happily. 😋</p>\n      <span class=\"story-piece\">✨ NEW POINT · Order food politely and say what you'll do!</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "goals", "html": "<div class=\"goals\">\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🍽️</span> Order food &amp; drinks at a restaurant</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">💡</span> -을게요 (I'll do ~) &amp; -을까요 (Shall I/we ~?)</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🔢</span> Count with 하나·두 개 + food vocabulary</div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "dialog", "html": "<div class=\"dialog\">\n    <div class=\"d-head\">\n      <span class=\"d-title\">💬 Dialogue 5 — Ordering Dinner</span>\n      <span class=\"d-scene\">🍜 Restaurant after the schedule</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">지우</div><div class=\"ko\">오늘 스케줄 끝났네요! 우리 무엇을 먹을까요?</div><div class=\"gl\">Today's schedule is over! What shall we eat?</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-05.webp\" alt=\"유나\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">유나</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 매운 떡볶이를 주문할게요!</div><div class=\"gl\">I'll order the spicy tteokbokki!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/m-01.webp\" alt=\"지훈\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">지훈</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 김밥 두 개를 주문할게요.</div><div class=\"gl\">I'll order two gimbap.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-02.webp\" alt=\"서연\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">서연</div><div class=\"ko\">이 메뉴는 맛있어요! 저도 하나를 먹을게요.</div><div class=\"gl\">This dish is delicious! I'll have one too.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/m-05.webp\" alt=\"하준\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">하준</div><div class=\"ko\">좋아요. 저는 계산을 할게요. 모두 맛있게 먹어요!</div><div class=\"gl\">Great. I'll pay the bill. Everyone, eat well!</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 1</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-을게요 / -ㄹ게요 — \"I'll do ~\" (friendly promise)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">To tell someone what <b>you will do</b> for them, add <b>-을게요</b> after a final consonant and <b>-ㄹ게요</b> after a vowel. It's a warm, friendly promise of your own action — perfect when ordering: <b>주문하다 → 주문할게요</b> = \"I'll order.\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">저는 지금 주문할게요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I'll order now. (주문하다 → 주문할게요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">제가 계산을 할게요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I'll pay the bill. (계산하다 → 할게요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">저는 떡볶이를 먹을게요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I'll eat tteokbokki. (받침 ㄱ → 을게요)</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 2</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-을까요? / -ㄹ까요? — \"Shall I/we ~?\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Add <b>-을까요?</b> (consonant) or <b>-ㄹ까요?</b> (vowel) to a verb to ask a friendly choice — \"Shall we …?\" or \"Shall I …?\" It asks the listener's opinion, so it's great in a restaurant: <b>무엇을 먹을까요?</b> = \"What shall we eat?\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">무엇을 먹을까요?</span><span class=\"gl\">What shall we eat?</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">제가 주문할까요?</span><span class=\"gl\">Shall I order?</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">우리 뭐를 마실까요?</span><span class=\"gl\">What shall we drink?</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 3</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">Counting 하나·두 개 + 주문하다 — \"one / two of them\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Native Korean numbers 하나(1), 둘(2), 셋(3), 넷(4), 다섯(5) shorten before the counter <b>개</b>: 하나→<b>한</b>, 둘→<b>두</b>, 셋→<b>세</b>. So 한 개 = one, 두 개 = two. To order, say [food] + <b>한/두 개</b> + 주세요.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">김밥 두 개 주세요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Please give me two gimbap.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">떡볶이 한 개를 주문할게요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I'll order one tteokbokki.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">음료수 세 개 주세요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Please give me three drinks.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "teach", "html": "<div class=\"teach\">\n  <span class=\"t-label\">🧑‍🏫 Teacher's Deep-Dive · Breaking down \"저는 매운 떡볶이를 주문할게요\"</span>\n  <div class=\"t-q\"><span class=\"t-ko\">저는 매운 떡볶이를 주문할게요.</span> <span class=\"t-en\">= \"I'll order the spicy tteokbokki.\"</span></div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-row t-head\">\n    <div class=\"t-why\">How does an idol order dinner in Korean? After a long schedule they walk into a 식당 (restaurant) and say what they'll get — the secret is a gentle ending right on the verb.</div>\n    <div class=\"t-deep\">\n      Korean doesn't use a separate word for \"will\" the way English does. Instead a small ending <b>-을게요/-ㄹ게요</b> is glued onto the verb to mean <b>\"I'll do ~\"</b> — a friendly promise of your own action. Our model verb <b>주문하다</b> (to order) ends in <b>-하다</b>; the stem <b>주문하</b> ends in a vowel, so we add <b>-ㄹ게요</b> → <span class=\"pt-ko\">주문할게요</span> = \"I'll order.\" Before that comes <span class=\"pt-ko\">매운 떡볶이를</span> — \"the spicy tteokbokki\" — with <b>을</b> marking it as the thing being ordered.\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-grid\">\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">저는</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">as for me <span class=\"t-sub\">(topic)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">저 = humble \"I\". <b>는</b> introduces who is doing the ordering.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">매운 떡볶이를</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">spicy tteokbokki <span class=\"t-sub\">(object)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\"><b>맵다</b> = spicy, and before a noun it becomes <b>매운</b>. <b>를</b> marks the dish as the object of \"order\".</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-eqcell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">주문할게요</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">I'll order <span class=\"t-sub\">(주문하다 + ㄹ게요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\"><b>주문하</b> ends in a vowel, so add <b>-ㄹ게요</b> = \"I'll order\". Compare <b>제가 계산을 할게요</b> — \"I'll pay the bill\".</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-insight\">\n    <b class=\"t-i-ko\">-을게요 = \"I'll do ~\"</b> — you tell someone what YOU will do. It's gentle and friendly, so idols say it a lot. Put it on the order: <b>떡볶이를 주문할게요</b> = \"I'll order tteokbokki\", <b>계산을 할게요</b> = \"I'll pay\".\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-compare\">\n    <div class=\"t-c-a\"><b>-을게요 → I'll do ~ (my promise)</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">저는 김밥 두 개를 주문할게요.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">\"I'll order two gimbap.\" — I'm telling you what I'll do.</span></div>\n    <div class=\"t-c-b\"><b>-을까요? → Shall we/I ~? (asking)</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">무엇을 먹을까요?</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">\"What shall we eat?\" — I'm asking your opinion.</span></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-tip\">\n    💡 <b>Memory tip:</b> decide yourself with <b>-을게요</b> (\"I'll do it\"), ask together with <b>-을까요?</b> (\"Shall we?\"). Ordering: <span class=\"pt-ko\">떡볶이 한 개를 주문할게요!</span> Just like Seoyeon at the restaurant!\n  </div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "vocab-lab", "html": "<div class=\"vocab-lab\"><div class=\"vl-toolbar\"><span class=\"vl-hint\">카테고리를 눌러 그림과 함께 공부하세요</span><button class=\"vl-expand\" onclick=\"glowVocabAll()\">모두 펼치기</button></div><div class=\"vl-cat open\" data-tone=\"sky\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🍽️</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">음식과 식당<small>Food & the restaurant · 뭐를 먹어요?</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">4</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a5_menu.webp\" alt=\"메뉴\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('메뉴')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">메뉴</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">menyu</div><div class=\"vw-en\">menu</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u5_food.webp\" alt=\"음식\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('음식')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">음식</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">eumsik</div><div class=\"vw-en\">food</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a5_restaurant.webp\" alt=\"식당\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('식당')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">식당</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">sikdang</div><div class=\"vw-en\">restaurant</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a5_price.webp\" alt=\"값\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('값')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">값</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">gap</div><div class=\"vw-en\">price</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('메뉴를 볼게요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">메뉴를 볼게요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I'll look at the menu.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('이 식당은 음식이 맛있어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">이 식당은 음식이 맛있어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">This restaurant's food is delicious.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('음식 값이 얼마예요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">음식 값이 얼마예요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">How much is the food?</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🍽️ <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 식당에서 음식과 메뉴를 봐요. 메뉴<b>를</b> 봐요 (look at the menu), 음식 값이 <b>얼마예요?</b> (How much?). 식당<b>에서</b> = \"at the restaurant\".</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"pink\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🌶️</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">맛의 말<small>Words for taste · 맵고 맛있어요</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">2</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u6_spicy.webp\" alt=\"맵다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('맵다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">맵다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">maepda</div><div class=\"vw-en\">spicy</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u6_delicious.webp\" alt=\"맛있다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('맛있다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">맛있다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">masitda</div><div class=\"vw-en\">delicious</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('이 떡볶이는 맵지만 맛있어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">이 떡볶이는 맵지만 맛있어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">This tteokbokki is spicy but delicious.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('매운 음식을 좋아해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">매운 음식을 좋아해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I like spicy food.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🌶️ <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 맵다 (spicy) → before a noun becomes <b>매운</b>: 매운 떡볶이. 맛있다 = \"it tastes good / delicious\".</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"lav\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🧾</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">주문과 계산<small>Ordering & the bill · 주문할게요</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">2</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a5_order.webp\" alt=\"주문\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('주문')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">주문</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">jumun</div><div class=\"vw-en\">order</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a5_bill.webp\" alt=\"계산\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('계산')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">계산</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">gyesan</div><div class=\"vw-en\">bill / paying</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저는 지금 주문할게요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">저는 지금 주문할게요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I'll order now.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('무엇을 주문할까요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">무엇을 주문할까요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">What shall we order?</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('계산은 제가 할게요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">계산은 제가 할게요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I'll pay the bill.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🧾 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 주문하다 → <b>주문할게요</b> (I'll order), <b>주문할까요?</b> (Shall I order?). 계산하다 → <b>계산을 할게요</b> (I'll pay).</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[5-1] Reading — 주문할게요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">지우: 저는 지금 주문할게요.</span> What does Jiwoo say?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a5q1\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a5q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> I'm ordering now.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a5q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> I ordered earlier.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a5q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> Can you order for me?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a5q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> I can't order.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a5q1\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The ending <b class=\"hl\">-ㄹ게요/-을게요</b> = <b class=\"hl\">\"I'll do ~\"</b> — a friendly promise of your own action. <b>주문하다 → 주문할게요</b> = \"I'll order\", so <span class=\"pt-ko\">저는 지금 주문할게요</span> means <b class=\"hl\">\"I'll order now\"</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ The others say past (\"ordered earlier\"), ask someone else to order, or say \"can't\" — none match the friendly <b>-을게요</b> ending.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Rule: friendly \"I'll do ~\" → <span class=\"pt-ko\">verb + 을게요/ㄹ게요</span>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[5-2] Reading — 무엇을 먹을까요?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose what the speaker is asking.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">하준: 우리 무엇을 먹을까요?</span> What is Hajun doing?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a5q2\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a5q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> He is eating now.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a5q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> He is asking what to eat.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a5q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> He ate already.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a5q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> He doesn't like food.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a5q2\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The ending <b class=\"hl\">-을까요?</b> turns a verb into a question about a choice. <b>먹다</b> (to eat) → <b>먹을까요?</b> = \"shall (we) eat?\" So <span class=\"pt-ko\">무엇을 먹을까요?</span> means <b class=\"hl\">\"What shall we eat?\"</b> — he's asking his friends.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ Eating now, eating before, and not liking food are all statements, but <b>-을까요?</b> is a question asking the listener's opinion.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Rule: ask a friendly \"shall we/I?\" → <span class=\"pt-ko\">verb + 을까요/ㄹ까요?</span></div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[5-3] Reading — 주문하다 + ㄹ게요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct ending for \"I'll order now\".</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">저는 지금 주문하(　).</span> Choose the polite future of 주문하다.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a5q3\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a5q3',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> ㄹ까요?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a5q3',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> ㄴ 수 있어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a5q3',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> ㄹ게요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a5q3',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 세요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a5q3\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The verb is <b class=\"hl\">주문하다</b>. Its stem <b>주문하</b> ends in a vowel, so we add <b class=\"hl\">-ㄹ게요</b> → <b>주문할게요</b> = \"I'll order.\" <b>주문할게요</b> is the friendly \"I'll do it\" form.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b>ㄹ까요?</b> is a question (\"Shall I?\"), <b>ㄴ 수 있어요</b> is wrong (the \"can\" form is ㄹ 수 있어요), and <b>세요</b> is a polite request to another person.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 주문하다 (vowel ending) → <span class=\"pt-ko\">주문할게요</span>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[5-4] Reading — Counting 한 개·두 개</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Which sentence correctly orders two gimbap?</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Choose the sentence that correctly says <span class=\"pt-ko\">\"two gimbap\"</span>.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a5q4\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a5q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 김밥 이 개 주세요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a5q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 김밥 둘 개 주세요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a5q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 김밥 두 개 주세요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a5q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 김밥 하나 주세요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a5q4\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Counting with <b class=\"hl\">개</b>: the native number <b>둘</b> (two) shortens to <b class=\"hl\">두</b> before a counter. So \"two gimbap\" = <span class=\"pt-ko\">김밥 두 개</span>, and to order: <b class=\"hl\">김밥 두 개 주세요</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b>이 개</b> uses the Chinese-style number (wrong with 개), <b>둘 개</b> keeps the full form (should be 두), and <b>하나 주세요</b> means just \"one\".</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 하나→한, 둘→두, 셋→세, 넷→네 before 개: 한 개, 두 개, 세 개, 네 개.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[5-5] Listening — how many?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Listen and choose how many bowls of rice the speaker orders.</div>\n\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('김치찌개 한 개하고 공기밥 두 개 주세요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">How many <span class=\"pt-ko\">공기밥</span> (bowls of rice) does the speaker order?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a5q5\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a5q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> one (한 개)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a5q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> two (두 개)<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a5q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> three (세 개)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a5q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> four (네 개)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a5q5\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The audio says <span class=\"pt-ko\">김치찌개 한 개하고 공기밥 두 개 주세요</span> — \"please give me one kimchi stew and <b class=\"hl\">two</b> bowls of rice.\" Listen for <b class=\"hl\">두 개</b> = two.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 한 개 is the stew, not the rice; 세 개 and 네 개 are three and four.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Count the dishes: <span class=\"pt-ko\">한 개</span> = one, <span class=\"pt-ko\">두 개</span> = two.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[5-6] Reading — replying to the server</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the best reply to the question.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">The server asks <span class=\"pt-ko\">무엇을 주문할까요?</span> What do you say?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a5q6\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a5q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 김치찌개 한 개를 주문할게요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a5q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 네, 저는 배가 불러요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a5q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 주문 주세요 주세요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a5q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 계산은 언제 해요?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a5q6\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The server asks <span class=\"pt-ko\">무엇을 주문할까요?</span> = \"What shall I take your order for?\" You answer by telling them what <b>you</b> will have: <b class=\"hl\">김치찌개 한 개를 주문할게요</b> = \"I'll order one kimchi stew.\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ Being full, nonsense repetition, and asking when to pay don't answer the server's \"what will you order?\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Reply to an ordering question with <span class=\"pt-ko\">○○ 한 개를 주문할게요</span>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[5-7] Reading — choose the wrong sentence</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Which sentence is NOT correct?</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Pick the sentence that has a mistake.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a5q7\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a5q7',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 저는 지금 주문할게요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a5q7',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 김치찌개 하나 주세요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a5q7',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 맥주 이 개 주세요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a5q7',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 제가 계산을 할게요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a5q7\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">For a portion you must use the <b class=\"hl\">native number + 개</b>: <b>하나→한 개</b>, <b>둘→두 개</b>. The Chinese-style number is wrong here, so <b class=\"hl\">맥주 이 개</b> is incorrect — it should be <span class=\"pt-ko\">맥주 두 개</span>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b>주문할게요</b> (I'll order), <b>하나 주세요</b> (please give one), and <b>계산을 할게요</b> (I'll pay) are all correct Korean.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Use native numbers with 개: 한/두/세/네 개, never 이 개.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[5-8] Listening — who will order?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Listen and choose who will order the food.</div>\n\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('지훈: 저는 주문을 할게요. 유나: 저는 계산을 할게요. 서연: 저는 먹을게요!')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Listen to the audio. Who will ORDER the food?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a5q8\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a5q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 지훈<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a5q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 유나<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a5q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 하준<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a5q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 서연<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a5q8\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The audio says <span class=\"pt-ko\">저는 주문을 할게요</span> (I'll do the ordering) spoken by <b class=\"hl\">지훈</b>, then <b>유나</b> says <span class=\"pt-ko\">저는 계산을 할게요</span> (I'll pay). The one who will <b>order</b> is <b class=\"hl\">지훈</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 유나 says she will pay (계산), not order. The other names are not the speakers.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Listen for who says <span class=\"pt-ko\">주문을 할게요</span> (order) vs <span class=\"pt-ko\">계산을 할게요</span> (pay).</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[5-9] Reading — order two bowls</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Which sentence correctly means <span class=\"pt-ko\">\"I'll order two gimbap\"</span>?</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Choose the correct sentence.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a5q9\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a5q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 김밥 한 개 주문할게요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a5q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 김밥 두 개 주문할게요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a5q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 김밥 두 개 주문할까요?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a5q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 김밥 둘 개 주문할게요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a5q9\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Put it together: count two as <b class=\"hl\">두 개</b>, and say \"I'll order\" as <b class=\"hl\">주문할게요</b>. So \"I'll order two gimbap\" = <span class=\"pt-ko\">김밥 두 개 주문할게요</span>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 한 개 is \"one\"; <b>주문할까요?</b> is a question (\"shall I order?\"), and <b>둘 개</b> uses the wrong full number form.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 두 개 (two) + 주문할게요 (I'll order) = a perfect restaurant order.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[5-10] Listening — the idol's evening</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Listen and choose the best summary.</div>\n\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('오늘 스케줄이 끝났어요. 그래서 지금 식당에서 저녁을 먹을게요. 저는 김치찌개 한 개를 주문할게요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">What is the speaker doing?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a5q10\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a5q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> Ordering dinner at a restaurant<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a5q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> Practicing a dance on stage<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a5q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> Buying shoes at a store<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a5q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> Cooking at home<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a5q10\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The speaker says today's schedule is done, so she is <b class=\"hl\">at a restaurant</b> and will eat dinner — <span class=\"pt-ko\">식당에서 저녁을 먹을게요</span> and <span class=\"pt-ko\">김치찌개 한 개를 주문할게요</span>. Best summary: <b class=\"hl\">ordering dinner at a restaurant</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ There's no dancing, no shoes, and she says she'll order food rather than cook it at home.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Catch the food words: <span class=\"pt-ko\">식당</span> (restaurant), <span class=\"pt-ko\">주문할게요</span> (I'll order), <span class=\"pt-ko\">한 개</span> (one).</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "culture", "html": "<div class=\"culture\">\n    <span class=\"c-label\">🎤 K-POP TIP</span>\n    <h3>Order Like a Star After the Show!</h3>\n    <p>When idols finish a schedule they're starving. They grab the menu and say what they'll have — 주문할게요! Polite, friendly, and hungry. Now YOU can order dinner in Korean too.</p>\n    <div class=\"c-tip\">✍️ \"저는 ○○ 한 개를 주문할게요!\" — \"I'll order one ○○!\" Or ask together: \"우리 무엇을 먹을까요?\" (\"What shall we eat?\")</div>\n  </div>"}]}, {"id": 6, "title": "How did you decide to spend vacation?", "en": "휴가를 어떻게 보내기로 했어요?", "theme": "vacation plans", "sections": [{"cls": "unit-flag", "html": "<div class=\"unit-flag\">UNIT 6 · VACATION PLANS</div>"}, {"cls": "sec-title", "html": "<div class=\"sec-title\"><div class=\"no\">6</div><div><h2>How did you decide to spend vacation?</h2><div class=\"en\">휴가를 어떻게 보내기로 했어요? — Vacation plans · -기로 하다 &amp; 어떻게</div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "story", "html": "<div class=\"story\">\n    <img class=\"story-art\" src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n    <div class=\"story-body\">\n      <span class=\"story-tag\">💿 GLOWSIS STORY · NEW SEASON · VACATION PLANS</span>\n      <h3>휴가 계획을 세워요 — \"어떻게 보내기로 했어요?\"</h3>\n      <p>긴 시즌이 끝나고 다섯 멤버가 <b>휴가</b>를 준비해요. <b>유나</b>는 바다로, <b>지훈</b>은 산으로… <b>하준</b>은 친구와 캠핑을 가기로 했어요. 그런데 막내 하준은 아직 <b>계획</b>을 못 정했어요! \"휴가를 어떻게 보내기로 했어요?\" 😎</p>\n      <p class=\"story-en\">After a long season the five members get ready for <b>vacation</b>. <b>Yuna</b> heads to the sea, <b>Jihoon</b> to the mountains… and <b>Hajun</b> decided to go camping with his friends. But the youngest, Hajun, hasn't made his <b>plan</b> yet! \"How did you decide to spend your vacation?\" 😎</p>\n      <span class=\"story-piece\">✨ NEW POINT · Say how you decided &amp; what you'll do!</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "goals", "html": "<div class=\"goals\">\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🗓️</span> Talk about plans &amp; decisions for vacation</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">✅</span> -기로 하다 (decide to) &amp; -(으)르 거예요 (will)</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🌊</span> Vacation &amp; travel vocabulary</div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "dialog", "html": "<div class=\"dialog\">\n    <div class=\"d-head\">\n      <span class=\"d-title\">💬 Dialogue 6 — Vacation Plans</span>\n      <span class=\"d-scene\">🏖️ Backstage after the final show</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">지우</div><div class=\"ko\">여러분, 시즌이 끝났어요! 휴가를 어떻게 보내기로 했어요?</div><div class=\"gl\">Everyone, the season is over! How did you decide to spend your vacation?</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-05.webp\" alt=\"유나\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">유나</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 바다에 가기로 했어요. 바닷가에서 쉼 거예요!</div><div class=\"gl\">I decided to go to the sea. I'll rest by the beach!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/m-01.webp\" alt=\"지훈\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">지훈</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 산에 가서 캠핑을 할 거예요. 자연이 좋아요.</div><div class=\"gl\">I'll go to the mountains and go camping. I love nature.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/m-05.webp\" alt=\"하준\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">하준</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 친구하고 여행을 가기로 했어요. 어떻게 결정했어요?</div><div class=\"gl\">I decided to go traveling with my friends. How did you decide?</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-02.webp\" alt=\"서연\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">서연</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 여행 계획을 세우기로 했어요. 다 같이 놀러 가요! 😂</div><div class=\"gl\">I decided to make a travel plan. Let's all go play together! 😂</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 1</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-기로 하다 — \"decide to\" (make up your mind)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">To say you <b>decided</b> to do something, add <b>-기로 하다</b> to a verb stem: verb stem + <b>-기로 했어요</b> = \"decided to…\". So 가다 (go) → 가<b>기로 했어요</b> = \"decided to go\".</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">저는 바다에 가기로 했어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I decided to go to the sea. (가다 → 가기로)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">유나는 집에서 쉼기로 했어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Yuna decided to rest at home. (쉼다 → 쉼기로)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">하준은 캠핑을 하기로 했어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Hajun decided to go camping. (하다 → 하기로)</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 2</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-(으)르 거예요 — \"I will / plan to\" (future)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">To say what you <b>will do</b>, add <b>-르 거예요</b> after a vowel and <b>-을 거예요</b> after a final consonant. It's the friendly \"going to\" for plans: 가다 → 갈 거예요 = \"I will go\".</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">지훈은 산에 갈 거예요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Jihoon will go to the mountain. (가다 → 갈 거예요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">저는 캠핑을 할 거예요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I will go camping. (하다 → 할 거예요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">서연은 친구를 만날 거예요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Seoyeon will meet a friend. (만나다 → 만날 거예요)</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 3</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">어떻게 — \"how\" (asking the way)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\"><b>어떻게</b> means <b>how</b>. Put it near the start of a question to ask how something happens or how you do it: 어떻게 보냈어요? = \"how did you spend it?\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">휴가를 어떻게 보내기로 했어요?</span><span class=\"gl\">How did you decide to spend your vacation?</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">어떻게 여행을 갈 거예요?</span><span class=\"gl\">How will you go traveling? (how + future)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">어떻게 결정했어요?</span><span class=\"gl\">How did you decide?</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "teach", "html": "<div class=\"teach\">\n  <span class=\"t-label\">🧑‍🏫 Teacher's Deep-Dive · Breaking down \"어떻게 보내기로 했어요?\"</span>\n  <div class=\"t-q\"><span class=\"t-ko\">휴가를 어떻게 보내기로 했어요?</span> <span class=\"t-en\">= \"How did you decide to spend your vacation?\"</span></div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-row t-head\">\n    <div class=\"t-why\">How do Korean idols say \"I <b>decided</b> to…\" and ask \"<b>how</b>?\" Vacation talk is all about plans!</div>\n    <div class=\"t-deep\">\n      When you make up your mind about a plan, Korean glues <b>-기로 하다</b> onto the verb — \"decide to (do)\". Today's model adds <b>어떻게</b> (how) to ask the plan:\n      <span class=\"pt-ko\">보내기로 했어요</span> = \"decided to spend\". Pair it with <span class=\"pt-ko\">-(으)르 거예요</span> (will) to say what comes next: <span class=\"pt-ko\">바다에 갈 거예요</span> = \"I'll go to the sea\".\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-grid\">\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">휴가를</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">vacation <span class=\"t-sub\">(object)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">휴가 = vacation/break. <b>을</b> marks it as the thing you \"spend\" (보내다).</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">어떻게</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">how <span class=\"t-sub\">(question word)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">어떻게 = how. Asks the <b>way</b> you do something — the manner, not the place.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-eqcell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">보내기로 했어요</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">decided to spend <span class=\"t-sub\">(보내다 + 기로 하다)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">보내다 = spend (time). Stem 보내 + <b>-기로 했어요</b> = \"decided to spend\".</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-insight\">\n    <b class=\"t-i-ko\">-기로 하다 = \"decide to\"</b> — take any verb stem and add <b>-기로 했어요</b> (decided) / <b>-기로 해요</b> (decide). <b>가기로 했어요</b> = decided to go, <b>하기로 했어요</b> = decided to do.\n    Put <b>어떻게</b> in front to ask <b>how</b> they decided.\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-compare\">\n    <div class=\"t-c-a\"><b>-기로 하다 → decide to (a choice you made)</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">저는 바다에 가기로 했어요.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">\"I decided to go to the sea.\" — a firm decision.</span></div>\n    <div class=\"t-c-b\"><b>-(으)르 거예요 → will (what you plan)</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">저는 바다에 갈 거예요.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">\"I will go to the sea.\" — your plan for the future.</span></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-tip\">\n    💡 <b>Memory tip:</b> first you <span class=\"pt-ko\">정하다/기로 하다</span> (decide), then you <span class=\"pt-ko\">-르 거예요</span> (do it). Ask a friend:\n    <span class=\"pt-ko\">어떻게 보내기로 했어요?</span> and answer <span class=\"pt-ko\">○○에 가기로 했어요!</span> Like planning an idol vacation!\n  </div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "vocab-lab", "html": "<div class=\"vocab-lab\"><div class=\"vl-toolbar\"><span class=\"vl-hint\">카테고리를 눈러 그림과 함께 공부하세요</span><button class=\"vl-expand\" onclick=\"glowVocabAll()\">모두 폼쳐보기</button></div><div class=\"vl-cat open\" data-tone=\"pink\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🧳</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">휴가와 여행<small>Vacation &amp; travel · 보내기로 했어요</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">4</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b14_vacation.webp\" alt=\"휴가\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('휴가')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">휴가</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">hyuga</div><div class=\"vw-en\">vacation / holiday</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b14_plan.webp\" alt=\"계획\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('계획')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">계획</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">gyehoek</div><div class=\"vw-en\">plan</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a6_decision.webp\" alt=\"결정\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('결정')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">결정</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">gyeoljeong</div><div class=\"vw-en\">decision</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b14_travel.webp\" alt=\"여행\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('여행')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">여행</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">yeohaeng</div><div class=\"vw-en\">travel / trip</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('휴가를 어떻게 보내기로 했어요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">휴가를 어떻게 보내기로 했어요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">How did you decide to spend your vacation?</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저는 여행 계획을 세웠어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">저는 여행 계획을 세웠어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I made a travel plan.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('어떻게 결정했어요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">어떻게 결정했어요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">How did you decide?</span></div></div></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"sky\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🏔️</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">바다, 산과 캠핑<small>Places &amp; activities · 어디로 갈까요?</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">4</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a6_sea.webp\" alt=\"바다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('바다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">바다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">bada</div><div class=\"vw-en\">sea / ocean</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a6_mountain.webp\" alt=\"산\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('산')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">산</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">san</div><div class=\"vw-en\">mountain</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a6_camping.webp\" alt=\"캠핑\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('캠핑')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">캠핑</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">kaemping</div><div class=\"vw-en\">camping</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u1_friend.webp\" alt=\"친구\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('친구')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">친구</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">chingu</div><div class=\"vw-en\">friend</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저는 바다에 갈 거예요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">저는 바다에 갈 거예요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I will go to the sea.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('친구하고 산에 가서 캠핑을 해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">친구하고 산에 가서 캠핑을 해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I go to the mountain with friends and camp.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('휴가를 어떻게 보낼 거예요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">휴가를 어떻게 보낼 거예요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">How will you spend your vacation?</span></div></div></div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[6-1] Reading — 휴가를 어떻게 보내기로 했어요]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">하준: 저는 친구하고 여행을 가기로 했어요.</span> What did Hajun decide?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a6q1\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a6q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> He decided to go traveling with his friends.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a6q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> He decided to go to school.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a6q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> He will rest at home.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a6q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> He can't go traveling.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a6q1\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The key phrase is <b class=\"hl\">여행을 가기로 했어요</b> = \"decided to go traveling\". <b class=\"hl\">-기로 하다</b> means \"decide to\", and <span class=\"pt-ko\">친구하고</span> = \"with friends\".</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">&#9312; going to school, resting at home, and \"can't\" (못) all add ideas that are not in the sentence.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Verb stem + <span class=\"pt-ko\">-기로 했어요</span> = \"decided to …\".</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[6-2] Reading — 바다에 갈 거예요]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">유나: 저는 바다에 갈 거예요.</span> What will Yuna do?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a6q2\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a6q2',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> She went to the sea yesterday.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a6q2',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> She can swim in the sea.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a6q2',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> She will go to the sea.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a6q2',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> She decided to stay home.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a6q2\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The ending <b class=\"hl\">-(으)르 거예요</b> = \"will / going to\". <b>가다 → 갈 거예요</b> = <b class=\"hl\">\"will go\"</b>, and <span class=\"pt-ko\">바다에</span> = \"to the sea\".</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">&#9312; \"went yesterday\" would be past <span class=\"pt-ko\">갔어요</span>, \"can\" uses <span class=\"pt-ko\">-르 수 있어요</span>, and staying home is a different place.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Future plan → <span class=\"pt-ko\">verb + -르/을 거예요</span>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[6-3] Reading — 어떻게 보내기로 했어요]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct word to complete the question.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">휴가를 ( 　 ) 보내기로 했어요?</span> (\"How did you decide to spend your vacation?\")</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a6q3\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a6q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 어디에<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a6q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 어떻게<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a6q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 누가<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a6q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 언제<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a6q3\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The question asks <b class=\"hl\">HOW</b> the vacation was spent, so we need <b class=\"hl\">어떻게</b> (how).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">&#9312; 어디에 = where, 누가 = who, 언제 = when — each asks a different thing.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 \"how\" (the manner/way) is <span class=\"pt-ko\">어떻게</span>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[6-4] Reading — 캠핑을 하기로 했어요]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Which sentence means \"Jihoon decided to go camping\"?</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Choose the correct sentence.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a6q4\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a6q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 지훈은 캠핑을 할 거예요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a6q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 지훈은 캠핑을 해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a6q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 지훈은 캠핑을 하기로 했어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a6q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 지훈은 캠핑을 좋아해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a6q4\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">\"decided to go camping\" uses <b class=\"hl\">-기로 하다</b>: <span class=\"pt-ko\">캠핑을 하기로 했어요</span>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">&#9312; <b class=\"hl\">할 거예요</b> = will camp (future, no decision), <b class=\"hl\">해요</b> = camps (present), <b class=\"hl\">좋아해요</b> = likes.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 decide to → <span class=\"pt-ko\">-기로 했어요</span>; will → <span class=\"pt-ko\">-르 거예요</span>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[6-5] Listening — what did she decide?]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Listen and choose what the speaker decided to do.</div>\n\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('저는 휴가에 바다에 가기로 했어요. 바닷가에서 쉼고 싶어요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">What did she decide?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a6q5\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a6q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> She decided to go to the mountain.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a6q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> She decided to go to the sea.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a6q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> She decided to go camping alone.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a6q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> She decided to stay home.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a6q5\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The audio says <span class=\"pt-ko\">저는 바다에 가기로 했어요</span> = \"I decided to go to the sea\". The decision verb is <b class=\"hl\">가기로 했어요</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">&#9312; mountain, camping alone, and staying home are not mentioned — she clearly says <b class=\"hl\">바다</b> (sea).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Listen for <span class=\"pt-ko\">-기로 했어요</span> to hear a decision.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[6-6] Reading — 어떻게 여행을 갈 거예요?]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">서연: 어떻게 여행을 갈 거예요?</span> What is Seoyeon asking?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a6q6\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a6q6',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> Where are you going?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a6q6',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> When are you going?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a6q6',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> How will you go traveling?<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a6q6',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> Who will go with you?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a6q6\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The question word <b class=\"hl\">어떻게</b> = \"how\". <span class=\"pt-ko\">여행을 갈 거예요</span> = \"will go traveling\", so she asks <b class=\"hl\">how</b> you will travel.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">&#9312; where = 어디, when = 언제, who = 누가 — all different question words.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <span class=\"pt-ko\">어떻게</span> asks the way/method.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[6-7] Reading — correct future form]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct future form of the verb.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">친구를 만나서 같이 ( 　 ).</span> (\"meet a friend and go together\")</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a6q7\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a6q7',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 갔어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a6q7',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 갑니다<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a6q7',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 갈 거예요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a6q7',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 가고 싶어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a6q7\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The verb is <b class=\"hl\">가다</b> (to go). For a future plan add <b class=\"hl\">-(으)르 거예요</b>: 가다 → <b class=\"hl\">갈 거예요</b> = \"will go\".</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">&#9312; 갔어요 is the past, 갑니다 is formal present, and 가고 싶어요 means \"want to go\".</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 가다 → <span class=\"pt-ko\">갈 거예요</span> (will go).</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[6-8] Listening — where will they go?]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Listen and choose where Jihoon decided to go.</div>\n\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('지훈은 산에 가서 캠핑을 할 거예요. 산에서 자연을 좋아해요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Where will Jihoon go?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a6q8\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a6q8',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 바다 (the sea)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a6q8',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 집 (home)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a6q8',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 산 (the mountain)<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a6q8',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 학교 (school)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a6q8\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The audio says <span class=\"pt-ko\">지훈은 산에 가서 캠핑을 할 거예요</span> — Jihoon will go to the <b class=\"hl\">mountain</b> and camp.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">&#9312; sea, home, and school are distractors not mentioned in the audio.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <span class=\"pt-ko\">산에 가서 캠핑을 할 거예요</span> = \"I'll go to the mountain and camp\".</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[6-9] Reading — choose the wrong sentence]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Which sentence is NOT correct?</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Pick the sentence that has a mistake.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a6q9\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a6q9',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 저는 바다에 가기로 했어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a6q9',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 서연은 친구를 만날 거예요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a6q9',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 어떻게 휴가를 보내기로 했어요?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a6q9',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 저는 캠핑을 하기로 거예요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a6q9\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">하기로 거예요</b> mixes two endings — <b>-기로 하다</b> and <b>-(으)르 거예요</b> — which is wrong. Use ONE: <span class=\"pt-ko\">하기로 했어요</span> (decided to do) or <span class=\"pt-ko\">할 거예요</span> (will do).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">&#9312; The other three are correct: decided to go to the sea, will meet a friend, and the how-question.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Never stack <span class=\"pt-ko\">-기로 하다</span> and <span class=\"pt-ko\">-르 거예요</span> together.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[6-10] Listening — the idol plan]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Listen and choose the best summary.</div>\n\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('저는 휴가에 친구하고 여행을 가기로 했어요. 같이 바다에 갈 거예요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">What does the speaker say about her vacation?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a6q10\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a6q10',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> She hasn't decided yet.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a6q10',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> She decided to rest at home.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a6q10',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> She will go camping alone.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a6q10',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> She decided to travel with friends.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a6q10\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The speaker says <span class=\"pt-ko\">친구하고 여행을 가기로 했어요</span> — she <b class=\"hl\">decided to travel with friends</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">&#9312; resting at home (집에서 쉼기), camping alone, and \"not decided\" all contradict the audio.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <span class=\"pt-ko\">친구하고 여행을 가기로 했어요</span> = \"I decided to go traveling with my friends\".</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "culture", "html": "<div class=\"culture\">\n    <span class=\"c-label\">🎤 K-POP TIP</span>\n    <h3>Plan Like a K-POP Idol!</h3>\n    <p>After a busy comeback season, idols finally rest. They decide where to go, who to meet, and how to recharge before the next stage. Talk about YOUR plan with -기로 하다 and -(으)르 거예요!</p>\n    <div class=\"c-tip\">✍️ \"저는 ○○에 가기로 했어요. ○○하고 쉼 거예요.\" — \"(I decided to go to ○○. I'll rest with ○○.)\"</div>\n  </div>"}]}, {"id": 7, "title": "Don't eat too much cold food", "en": "찬 음식을 너무 많이 먹지 마세요", "theme": "advice", "sections": [{"cls": "unit-flag", "html": "<div class=\"unit-flag\">UNIT 7 · ADVICE</div>"}, {"cls": "sec-title", "html": "<div class=\"sec-title\"><div class=\"no\">7</div><div><h2>Don't eat too much cold food</h2><div class=\"en\">찬 음식을 너무 많이 먹지 마세요 — Advice · -지 마세요 · 너무 많이/조금 · -으면 좋겠다</div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "story", "html": "<div class=\"story\">\n    <img class=\"story-art\" src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n    <div class=\"story-body\">\n      <span class=\"story-tag\">💿 GLOWSIS STORY · NEW SEASON · ADVICE</span>\n      <h3>아이돌 건강 지키기 — 너무 많이 먹지 마세요!</h3>\n      <p>멤버들이 컴백 준비를 하며 찬 음식을 정말 많이 먹어요. 아이스크림, 냉면, 찬물… 다 너무 맛있어요! 그런데 <b>하준</b>의 <b>배</b>가 아파졌어요. 아이스크림을 너무 많이 먹지 마세요! 팜들이 걱정해요. 아이돌이 병원에 가면 안 되죠. <b>건강</b>이 제일 중요해요. …위가 아파요. 흡!</p>\n      <p class=\"story-en\">While getting ready for a comeback, the members eat a LOT of cold food. Ice cream, cold noodles, cold water… it's all too delicious! But then <b>Hajun's</b> <b>belly</b> starts to hurt. \"Don't eat too much ice cream!\" the fans worry. An idol can't get sick! <b>Health</b> is the most important thing. …My stomach hurts. Hm! 😭</p>\n      <span class=\"story-piece\">✨ NEW POINT · Give friendly advice about food &amp; health!</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "goals", "html": "<div class=\"goals\">\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🙅</span> Tell someone not to do something (-지 마세요)</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">⚖️</span> 너무 많이 (too much) vs 조금 (a little)</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">💚</span> Hope &amp; wish with -으면 좋겠다 · health words</div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "dialog", "html": "<div class=\"dialog\">\n    <div class=\"d-head\">\n      <span class=\"d-title\">💬 Dialogue 7 — Health Check</span>\n      <span class=\"d-scene\">🎹 Idol practice room</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">지우</div><div class=\"ko\">여러분, 아이스크림을 너무 많이 먹지 마세요!</div><div class=\"gl\">Everyone, don't eat too much ice cream!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/m-05.webp\" alt=\"하준\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">하준</div><div class=\"ko\">네, 알겠어요. 찬 음식을 조금만 먹을게요.</div><div class=\"gl\">Yes, I understand. I'll only eat a little cold food.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-02.webp\" alt=\"서연\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">서연</div><div class=\"ko\">하준아, 배가 아파요?</div><div class=\"gl\">Hajun, does your belly hurt?</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/m-05.webp\" alt=\"하준\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">하준</div><div class=\"ko\">네, 위가 조금 아파요. 찬 음식은 조금만 먹을게요.</div><div class=\"gl\">Yes, my stomach hurts a little. I'll only eat a little cold food.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-05.webp\" alt=\"유나\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">유나</div><div class=\"ko\">건강을 조심하세요! 팜들도 우리가 건강하면 좋겠어요!</div><div class=\"gl\">Please take care of your health! Fans hope we're healthy too!</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 1</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-지 마세요 — &quot;Don't do&hellip;&quot; (polite)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">To tell someone politely <b>NOT to do</b> something, add <b>-지 마세요</b> to the verb stem. 먹다 (eat) → 먹<b>지 마세요</b> = &quot;don't eat&quot;. It's the friendly, everyday way to give a warning or advice.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">찬 음식을 너무 많이 먹지 마세요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Don't eat too much cold food. (먹다 → 먹지 마세요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">늦게 자지 마세요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Don't go to bed late.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">너무 많이 마시지 마세요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Don't drink too much.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 2</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">너무 많이 / 조금 — &quot;too much&quot; vs &quot;a little&quot;</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">많이 = &quot;a lot&quot;. Add <b>너무</b> to make it <b>너무 많이</b> = &quot;too much&quot; (more than is good for you!). <b>조금</b> = &quot;a little&quot;, and <b>조금만</b> = &quot;only a little&quot;. Use them to talk about how much food is okay.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">아이스크림을 너무 많이 먹어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I eat too much ice cream.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">찬 음식을 조금만 먹어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I only eat a little cold food.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">너무 많이 먹으면 배가 아파요.</span><span class=\"gl\">If you eat too much, your belly hurts.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 3</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-으면 좋겠다 — &quot;I hope / I wish&hellip;&quot;</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">To say you <b>hope</b> or <b>wish</b> something, add <b>-으면 좋겠어요</b> after a verb/adjective that ends in a final consonant and <b>-면 좋겠어요</b> after a vowel. Add <b>안</b> or <b>지 않</b> to hope something does NOT happen.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">건강하면 좋겠어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I hope (you) are healthy. (건강하다 → 건강하면 좋겠어요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">찬 음식을 조금만 먹으면 좋겠어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I hope you only eat a little cold food. (먹다 → 먹으면)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">아프지 않으면 좋겠어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I hope you don't get sick.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "teach", "html": "<div class=\"teach\">\n  <span class=\"t-label\">🧑‍💻 Teacher's Deep-Dive · Breaking down &quot;찬 음식을 너무 많이 먹지 마세요&quot;</span>\n  <div class=\"t-q\"><span class=\"t-ko\">찬 음식을 너무 많이 먹지 마세요.</span> <span class=\"t-en\">= &quot;Don't eat too much cold food.&quot;</span></div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-row t-head\">\n    <div class=\"t-why\">How do you tell an idol (or a friend) <b>NOT</b> to do something? And how do fans say they <b>hope</b> the idols stay healthy? Korean has tidy endings for both.</div>\n    <div class=\"t-deep\">\n      English uses a separate word &quot;don't&quot;. Korean instead glues a tiny ending onto the verb: <b>-지 마세요</b> turns any verb into a polite &quot;please don't do it&quot;. Today's model sentence takes <span class=\"pt-ko\">먹다</span> (eat) → <b>먹지 마세요</b> (&quot;don't eat&quot;). The word <span class=\"pt-ko\">너무 많이</span> (too much) tells us HOW MUCH not to eat: <span class=\"pt-ko\">너무 많이 먹지 마세요</span> = &quot;don't eat too much&quot;. Simple, warm, and very common in real K-drama advice!\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-grid\">\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">찬</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">cold <span class=\"t-sub\">(adjective)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">찬 = &quot;cold&quot;. It describes the food — from 차갑다, &quot;to be cold&quot;.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">음식을</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">food <span class=\"t-sub\">(object)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">음식 = &quot;food&quot;. <b>을</b> marks it as the object of the verb &quot;eat&quot;.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">너무 많이</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">too much <span class=\"t-sub\">(amount)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">많이 = &quot;a lot&quot;. Add <b>너무</b> (too) → <b>너무 많이</b> = &quot;too much&quot;. The opposite is <b>조금</b>, &quot;a little&quot;.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-eqcell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">먹지 마세요</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">don't eat <span class=\"t-sub\">(-지 마세요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">Verb stem <b>먹</b> + <b>-지 마세요</b> = &quot;please don't eat&quot;. This ending is the polite way to stop someone.</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-insight\">\n    <b class=\"t-i-ko\">verb stem + 지 마세요 = &quot;don't do&hellip;&quot;</b> — put <b>-지 마세요</b> after any verb stem to forbid it politely: <b>먹지 마세요</b> (don't eat), <b>마시지 마세요</b> (don't drink), <b>늦게 자지 마세요</b> (don't sleep late). Pair it with <b>너무 많이</b> to say &quot;don't do it too much&quot;.\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-compare\">\n    <div class=\"t-c-a\"><b>-지 마세요 → don't (a warning)</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">너무 많이 먹지 마세요.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">&quot;Don't eat too much.&quot; — stop a bad habit.</span></div>\n    <div class=\"t-c-b\"><b>-으면 좋겠다 → I hope / wish</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">건강하면 좋겠어요.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">&quot;I hope you're healthy.&quot; — fans' warm wish for idols.</span></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-tip\">\n    💡 <b>Memory tip:</b> health talk has three helpers — <b>-지 마세요</b> (don't do), <b>너무 많이 / 조금</b> (too much / a little), and <b>-으면 좋겠어요</b> (I hope). Text a worried fan:\n    <span class=\"pt-ko\">너무 많이 먹지 마세요! 건강하면 좋겠어요!</span> (&quot;Don't eat too much! I hope you're healthy!&quot;)\n  </div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "vocab-lab", "html": "<div class=\"vocab-lab\"><div class=\"vl-toolbar\"><span class=\"vl-hint\">카테고리를 눌러 그림과 함께 공부하세요</span><button class=\"vl-expand\" onclick=\"glowVocabAll()\">모두 펼치기</button></div><div class=\"vl-cat open\" data-tone=\"sky\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🥶</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">찬 음식<small>Cold food &amp; eating · 뭐를 먹어요?</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">2</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a7_coldfood.webp\" alt=\"찬\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('찬')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">찬</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">chan</div><div class=\"vw-en\">cold (food)</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u5_food.webp\" alt=\"음식\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('음식')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">음식</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">eumsik</div><div class=\"vw-en\">food</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('찬 음식을 너무 많이 먹지 마세요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">찬 음식을 너무 많이 먹지 마세요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Don't eat too much cold food.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('찬 음식은 정말 맛있어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">찬 음식은 정말 맛있어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Cold food is really delicious.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('찬 음식은 조금만 먹어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">찬 음식은 조금만 먹어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I only eat a little cold food.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🥶 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 찬 = cold + 음식 = food. 먹다 (eat) takes -지 마세요 to warn: 먹<b>지 마세요</b> = &quot;don't eat&quot;.</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"pink\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">⚖️</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">얼마나<small>How much · 많이 vs 조금</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">2</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a7_alot.webp\" alt=\"많이\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('많이')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">많이</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">manhi</div><div class=\"vw-en\">a lot</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a10_alittle.webp\" alt=\"조금\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('조금')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">조금</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">jogeum</div><div class=\"vw-en\">a little</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('아이스크림을 너무 많이 먹지 마세요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">아이스크림을 너무 많이 먹지 마세요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Don't eat too much ice cream.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저는 조금만 먹어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">저는 조금만 먹어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I only eat a little.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('너무 많이 먹으면 배가 아파요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">너무 많이 먹으면 배가 아파요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">If you eat too much, your belly hurts.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">⚖️ <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 많이 = a lot · 조금 = a little. 너무 = too → <b>너무 많이</b> = too much. 조금<b>만</b> = only a little.</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"lav\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🩺</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">건강과 몸<small>Health &amp; the body · 잘 지내요</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">4</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b15_health.webp\" alt=\"건강\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('건강')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">건강</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">geongang</div><div class=\"vw-en\">health</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a7_stomach.webp\" alt=\"위\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('위')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">위</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">wi</div><div class=\"vw-en\">stomach</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a7_belly.webp\" alt=\"배\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('배')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">배</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">bae</div><div class=\"vw-en\">belly</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a7_careful.webp\" alt=\"조심\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('조심')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">조심</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">josim</div><div class=\"vw-en\">careful / beware</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('위가 아파요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">위가 아파요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">My stomach hurts.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('배가 아파요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">배가 아파요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">My belly hurts.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('건강을 조심하세요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">건강을 조심하세요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Please take care of your health.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('건강하면 좋겠어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">건강하면 좋겠어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I hope you are healthy.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🩺 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 위 = the stomach (organ) · 배 = the belly. 건강 = health. 조심하다 + -세요 = take care! 💚</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\"><div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[1] 찬 음식을 너무 많이 먹지 마세요</span></div><div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct meaning.</div><div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">지우: 찬 음식을 너무 많이 먹지 마세요.</span> What does Jiwoo say?</div><div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a7q1\"><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a7q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> Eat a lot of cold food.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a7q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> Don't eat too much cold food.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a7q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> Cold food is too expensive.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a7q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> Please make some cold food.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button></div><div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a7q1\"></div><div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍💻 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The words <b class=\"hl\">먹지 마세요</b> mean <b class=\"hl\">&quot;don't eat&quot;</b> (-지 마세요 = don't). <b>너무 많이</b> = too much, so the sentence is <span class=\"pt-ko\">찬 음식을 너무 많이 먹지 마세요</span> = <b class=\"hl\">&quot;Don't eat too much cold food&quot;</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The other answers talk about eating a lot, price, or cooking — none are in the sentence.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Rule: verb stem + <span class=\"pt-ko\">-지 마세요</span> = &quot;please don't&hellip;&quot;.</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\"><div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[2] 먹지 마세요 (-지 마세요)</span></div><div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct polite &quot;don't&quot; form.</div><div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">배가 아파요. 찬 음식을 (　).</span></div><div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a7q2\"><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a7q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 먹어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a7q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 먹지 마세요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a7q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 먹고 싶어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a7q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 먹을 거예요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button></div><div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a7q2\"></div><div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍💻 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">My belly hurts, so the advice is <b class=\"hl\">not to eat</b> cold food. The polite negative ending is <span class=\"pt-ko\">먹지 마세요</span> (&quot;don't eat&quot;).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">먹어요 (eat), 먹고 싶어요 (want to eat), and 먹을 거예요 (will eat) all say the opposite — they don't warn against eating.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Rule: verb stem <b class=\"hl\">먹</b> + <b class=\"hl\">-지 마세요</b> = &quot;don't eat&quot;.</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\"><div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[3] 너무 많이 (too much)</span></div><div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the meaning of 너무 많이.</div><div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">지훈: 저는 커피를 너무 많이 마셔요.</span> What does 너무 많이 mean?</div><div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a7q3\"><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a7q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> a little<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a7q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> too much<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a7q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> never<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a7q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> sometimes<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button></div><div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a7q3\"></div><div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍💻 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">많이 = <b class=\"hl\">&quot;a lot&quot;</b>. Add 너무 (&quot;too&quot;) → <b class=\"hl\">너무 많이</b> = &quot;too much&quot;. Jihoon drinks coffee <b>too much</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">a little is 조금, never is an 안/못 idea, sometimes is another word — none match.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Rule: <span class=\"pt-ko\">너무 많이</span> = too much (more than is good for you).</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\"><div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[4] 조금만 (a little)</span></div><div class=\"p-dir\">Fill in the blank with the right word.</div><div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">위가 아파요. 찬 음식을 (　)만 먹어요.</span></div><div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a7q4\"><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a7q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 많이<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a7q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 조금<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a7q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 건강<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a7q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 배<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button></div><div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a7q4\"></div><div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍💻 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">If my stomach hurts, I should eat <b class=\"hl\">only a little</b> cold food. The word for &quot;a little&quot; is <b class=\"hl\">조금</b>, and 조금<b>만</b> = &quot;only a little&quot;.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">많이 (a lot) would make it worse, and 건강/배 (health/belly) are nouns, not amounts.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Rule: <span class=\"pt-ko\">많이</span> (a lot) vs <span class=\"pt-ko\">조금만</span> (only a little).</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\"><div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[5] 왜 찬 음식을 먹지 마세요?</span></div><div class=\"p-dir\">Listen and answer.</div><button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('배가 아파요. 찬 음식을 많이 먹지 마세요.')\">🔊 Listen</button><div class=\"p-q\">Why shouldn't the person eat cold food?</div><div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a7q5\"><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a7q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> Because it is delicious.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a7q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> Because their belly hurts.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a7q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> Because it is expensive.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a7q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> Because they are full.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button></div><div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a7q5\"></div><div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍💻 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The audio says <span class=\"pt-ko\">배가 아파요</span> = &quot;my belly hurts&quot;, so the reason is <b class=\"hl\">their belly hurts</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Then it warns <span class=\"pt-ko\">찬 음식을 많이 먹지 마세요</span> = &quot;don't eat a lot of cold food&quot;.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Listen for <span class=\"pt-ko\">아파요</span> (hurts) to find the cause of the warning.</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\"><div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[6] -으면 좋겠다 (hope)</span></div><div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose what the fans hope.</div><div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">팬: 아이돌이 건강하면 좋겠어요.</span> What do the fans hope?</div><div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a7q6\"><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a7q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> They hope the idols are healthy.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a7q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> They hope the idols eat cold food.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a7q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> The fans are sick.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a7q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> The fans don't like idols.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button></div><div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a7q6\"></div><div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍💻 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">건강하면 좋겠어요</span> = <b class=\"hl\">&quot;I hope (they) are healthy&quot;</b>. 건강하다 → 건강하<b>면</b> 좋겠어요.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The sentence has no cold food, no sick fans, and no dislike — only a healthy hope.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Rule: <span class=\"pt-ko\">-으면 좋겠다 / -면 좋겠다</span> = &quot;I hope / I wish&hellip;&quot;.</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\"><div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[7] 어느 문장이 틀렸어요?</span></div><div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the sentence that is NOT correct.</div><div class=\"p-q\">Pick the sentence that has a mistake.</div><div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a7q7\"><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a7q7',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 찬 음식을 많이 먹지 마세요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a7q7',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 저는 찬 음식을 조금만 먹어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a7q7',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 건강을 조심하세요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a7q7',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 찬 음식을 먹지 마세요 못 해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button></div><div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a7q7\"></div><div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍💻 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">You can't stack <b class=\"hl\">-지 마세요</b> (don't) and <b class=\"hl\">못 해요</b> (can't) together — <span class=\"pt-ko\">먹지 마세요 못 해요</span> is not a real sentence.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The other three are correct: &quot;don't eat a lot of cold food&quot;, &quot;I only eat a little cold food&quot;, and &quot;please take care of your health&quot;.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Rule: use <span class=\"pt-ko\">-지 마세요</span> OR <span class=\"pt-ko\">못 해요</span>, never both.</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\"><div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[8] 누가 찬 음식을 너무 많이 먹어요?</span></div><div class=\"p-dir\">Listen and choose who eats too much cold food.</div><button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('유나는 건강을 잘 조심해요. 그런데 하준은 찬 음식을 너무 많이 먹어요.')\">🔊 Listen</button><div class=\"p-q\">Who eats too much cold food?</div><div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a7q8\"><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a7q8',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 유나<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a7q8',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 지우<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a7q8',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 하준<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a7q8',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 서연<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button></div><div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a7q8\"></div><div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍💻 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The audio: <span class=\"pt-ko\">유나는 건강을 잘 조심해요</span> (Yuna takes good care of her health), <b>but</b> <span class=\"pt-ko\">하준은 찬 음식을 너무 많이 먹어요</span> = Hajun eats too much cold food. So the answer is <b class=\"hl\">하준</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Yuna is the careful one — Jiwoo and Seoyeon are not mentioned.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Listen for <span class=\"pt-ko\">그런데</span> (&quot;but&quot;) — the contrast points to the answer.</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\"><div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[9] 친구에게 조언을 해요</span></div><div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the best advice for the situation.</div><div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">지우: 요즘 배가 자주 아파요.</span> Choose the best advice.</div><div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a7q9\"><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a7q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 찬 음식을 너무 많이 먹지 마세요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a7q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 너무 많이 먹어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a7q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 찬 음식을 많이 주세요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a7q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 위가 아파요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button></div><div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a7q9\"></div><div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍💻 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Jiwoo's belly often hurts, so the best advice is a friendly warning: <b class=\"hl\">찬 음식을 너무 많이 먹지 마세요</b> = &quot;don't eat too much cold food&quot;.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">너무 많이 먹어요 (&quot;eat too much&quot;) encourages the bad habit; asking for more cold food is wrong; &quot;my stomach hurts&quot; restates the problem instead of advising.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Rule: give advice with <span class=\"pt-ko\">-지 마세요</span> = &quot;don't&hellip;&quot;.</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\"><div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[10] 팬들의 마음</span></div><div class=\"p-dir\">Listen and choose what the fans want.</div><button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('팜들은 아이돌이 건강하면 좋겠어요. 찬 음식은 조금만 먹으면 좋겠어요.')\">🔊 Listen</button><div class=\"p-q\">What do the fans want for the idols?</div><div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a7q10\"><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a7q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> They want the idols to be healthy.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a7q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> They want the idols to eat cold food.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a7q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> They want the idols to eat a lot.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a7q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> They want the idols to go home.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button></div><div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a7q10\"></div><div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍💻 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The audio says <span class=\"pt-ko\">팬들은 아이돌이 건강하면 좋겠어요</span> = fans <b class=\"hl\">hope the idols are healthy</b> — the best summary.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">It also adds <span class=\"pt-ko\">찬 음식은 조금만 먹으면 좋겠어요</span> (hope they eat only a little cold food) — so eating a lot or more cold food is the opposite.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Rule: <span class=\"pt-ko\">-으면 좋겠어요</span> = &quot;I hope&hellip;&quot;. Fans always want the healthy choice.</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "culture", "html": "<div class=\"culture\">\n    <span class=\"c-label\">🎤 K-POP TIP</span>\n    <h3>Take Care of Your Idols’ Health!</h3>\n    <p>During comeback season idols practice hard and often eat quickly or too much. Real fans (and moms!) always worry: “Eat well, sleep well, and don’t eat too much cold food!” Use -지 마세요 to give warm, friendly warnings — and -으면 좋겠어요 to tell someone you hope they stay healthy.</p>\n    <div class=\"c-tip\">✍️ &quot;○○를 너무 많이 먹지 마세요! 건강하면 좋겠어요!&quot; — “Don’t eat too much ○○! I hope you’re healthy!&quot;</div>\n  </div>"}]}, {"id": 8, "title": "What do you want to do tonight?", "en": "오늘 저녁에 뭐 할래요?", "theme": "evening plans", "sections": [{"cls": "unit-flag", "html": "<div class=\"unit-flag\">UNIT 8 · EVENING PLANS</div>"}, {"cls": "sec-title", "html": "<div class=\"sec-title\"><div class=\"no\">8</div><div><h2>What do you want to do tonight?</h2><div class=\"en\">오늘 저녁에 뭐 할래요? — Evening plans · -을래요? &amp; 같이</div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "story", "html": "<div class=\"story\">\n    <img class=\"story-art\" src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n    <div class=\"story-body\">\n      <span class=\"story-tag\">💿 GLOWSIS STORY · NEW SEASON · EVENING PLANS</span>\n      <h3>오늘 저녁 계획을 세워요 — \"뭐 할래요?\"</h3>\n      <p>연습이 끝나고 다섯 멤버가 저녁에 뭘 할지 이야기해요. <b>지우</b>가 제일 먼저 물어봐요! \"오늘 저녁에 <b>뭐 할래요</b>?\" <b>유나</b>는 영화를 보고 싶고, <b>하준</b>은 같이 밥을 먹고 싶어요. <b>지훈</b>은 <b>노래방</b>에 가고 싶어 해요. 다들 약속을 정할까요? 😆</p>\n      <p class=\"story-en\">After practice ends, the five members talk about what to do tonight. <b>Jiwoo</b> asks first! \"What do you want to do <b>tonight</b>?\" <b>Yuna</b> wants to watch a movie, and <b>Hajun</b> wants to eat together. <b>Jihoon</b> wants to go to the <b>noraebang</b>. Shall they all make a plan? 😆</p>\n      <span class=\"story-piece\">✨ NEW POINT · Invite &amp; suggest plans for the evening!</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "goals", "html": "<div class=\"goals\">\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🌙</span> Make plans &amp; invite friends for tonight</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">✅</span> -을래요?/-ㄹ래요? (want to ~) &amp; 같이 (together)</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🎤</span> -(으)ㄹ까요? (shall we) &amp; evening activity vocabulary</div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "dialog", "html": "<div class=\"dialog\">\n    <div class=\"d-head\">\n      <span class=\"d-title\">💬 Dialogue 8 — Evening Plans</span>\n      <span class=\"d-scene\">🌆 After practice, at the practice room</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">지우</div><div class=\"ko\">여러분, 연습 끝났어요! 오늘 저녁에 뭐 할래요?</div><div class=\"gl\">Everyone, practice is over! What do you want to do tonight?</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-05.webp\" alt=\"유나\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">유나</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 영화를 보고 싶어요. 같이 영화를 볼래요?</div><div class=\"gl\">I want to watch a movie. Do you want to watch a movie together?</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/m-01.webp\" alt=\"지훈\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">지훈</div><div class=\"ko\">좋아요! 그런데 저는 노래방에 가고 싶어요. 노래방에 갈까요?</div><div class=\"gl\">OK! But I want to go to the noraebang. Shall we go to the noraebang?</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/m-05.webp\" alt=\"하준\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">하준</div><div class=\"ko\">저녁을 먼저 먹을래요! 배가 고파요. 같이 먹을래요?</div><div class=\"gl\">I want to eat dinner first! I am hungry. Do you want to eat together?</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-02.webp\" alt=\"서연\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">서연</div><div class=\"ko\">좋아요! 몇 시에 만날까요? 오늘 약속이 없어요. 😂</div><div class=\"gl\">Great! What time shall we meet? I have no plans today. 😂</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 1</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-을래요? / -ㄹ래요? — \"want to ~\" (casual, to a friend)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">To ask or say what you <b>want to do</b> with a friend, add <b>-을래요?</b> after a final consonant and <b>-ㄹ래요?</b> after a vowel: verb stem + <b>-을래요?/-ㄹ래요?</b> = \"want to ~\". So 하다 (do) → 하<b>ㄹ래요?</b> = \"want to do?\".</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">오늘 저녁에 뭐 할래요?</span><span class=\"gl\">What do you want to do tonight? (하다 → 할래요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">같이 영화를 볼래요?</span><span class=\"gl\">Do you want to watch a movie together? (보다 → 볼래요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">저녁을 먹을래요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I want to eat dinner. (먹다 → 먹을래요)</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 2</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">같이 — \"together\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\"><b>같이</b> means <b>together</b>. Put it before the verb to invite someone to join you: 같이 영화를 볼래요? = \"do you want to watch a movie <b>together</b>?\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">같이 저녁을 먹을래요?</span><span class=\"gl\">Do you want to eat dinner together?</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">같이 노래방에 갈까요?</span><span class=\"gl\">Shall we go to the noraebang together?</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">친구와 같이 시간을 보내요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I spend time together with a friend.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 3</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-(으)ㄹ까요? — \"shall we ~?\" (a soft suggestion)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">To <b>suggest</b> doing something together, add <b>-ㄹ까요?</b> after a vowel and <b>-을까요?</b> after a consonant: 가다 (go) → 가<b>ㄹ까요?</b> = \"shall we go?\". It is a gentle way to propose a plan.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">노래방에 갈까요?</span><span class=\"gl\">Shall we go to the noraebang? (가다 → 갈까요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">몇 시에 만날까요?</span><span class=\"gl\">What time shall we meet? (만나다 → 만날까요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">같이 산책할까요?</span><span class=\"gl\">Shall we take a walk together? (산책하다 → 산책할까요)</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "teach", "html": "<div class=\"teach\">\n  <span class=\"t-label\">🧑‍🏫 Teacher's Deep-Dive · Breaking down \"오늘 저녁에 뭐 할래요?\"</span>\n  <div class=\"t-q\"><span class=\"t-ko\">오늘 저녁에 뭐 할래요?</span> <span class=\"t-en\">= \"What do you want to do tonight?\"</span></div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-row t-head\">\n    <div class=\"t-why\">Practice just ended and the members are hungry for fun! How does a K-POP idol ask a friend <b>\"Do you want to ~?\"</b> The answer is the super-casual ending <b>-을래요?</b></div>\n    <div class=\"t-deep\">\n      In English we say \"want to + verb\". Korean squeezes it onto the end of the verb with <b>-을래요? / -ㄹ래요?</b> (want to, casual &amp; friendly). Add <b>-을래요</b> after a final consonant and <b>-ㄹ래요</b> after a vowel.\n      To ask what someone wants to do we say <span class=\"pt-ko\">뭐 할래요?</span> = \"what do you want to do?\". Add <b>같이</b> (together) to invite: <span class=\"pt-ko\">같이 영화를 볼래요?</span> = \"do you want to watch a movie together?\"\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-grid\">\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">오늘 저녁에</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">tonight <span class=\"t-sub\">(time)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\"><b>오늘</b> = today, <b>저녁</b> = evening/dinner. <b>에</b> marks the time: \"tonight\".</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">뭐</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">what <span class=\"t-sub\">(question word)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">Short for 무엇 — \"what\". It often sits right before the verb.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-eqcell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">할래요?</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">want to do? <span class=\"t-sub\">(하다 + ㄹ래요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\"><b>하다</b> → <b>할래요?</b> \"do you want to do?\". Same ending means \"I want to\": <b>밥을 먹을래요</b> = \"I want to eat.\"</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-insight\">\n    <b class=\"t-i-ko\">-을래요? / -ㄹ래요? = \"want to ~\"</b> — the friendly way to ask or say what you want to do. After a consonant <b>-을래요</b> (먹다 → <b>먹을래요</b>), after a vowel <b>-ㄹ래요</b> (하다 → <b>할래요</b>). Pair it with <b>같이</b> (together) to invite a friend to join you.\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-compare\">\n    <div class=\"t-c-a\"><b>-을래요? → \"do you want to ~?\" (ask a friend)</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">같이 영화를 볼래요?</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">\"Do you want to watch a movie together?\"</span></div>\n    <div class=\"t-c-b\"><b>-(으)ㄹ까요? → \"shall we ~?\" (let's decide together)</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">노래방에 갈까요?</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">\"Shall we go to the noraebang?\" — a soft suggestion.</span></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-tip\">\n    💡 <b>Memory tip:</b> ask a friend <span class=\"pt-ko\">오늘 저녁에 뭐 할래요?</span> (\"what do you want to do tonight?\"). They answer <span class=\"pt-ko\">영화를 볼래요!</span> (\"I want to watch a movie!\") and you say <span class=\"pt-ko\">좋아요, 같이 봐요!</span> (\"OK, let's watch together!\"). 노래방, 산책, 영화 — pick your plan!\n  </div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "vocab-lab", "html": "<div class=\"vocab-lab\"><div class=\"vl-toolbar\"><span class=\"vl-hint\">카테고리를 눌러 그림과 함께 공부하세요</span><button class=\"vl-expand\" onclick=\"glowVocabAll()\">모두 펼치기</button></div><div class=\"vl-cat open\" data-tone=\"sky\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🎬</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">오늘 저녁 활동<small>Tonight's plans · 뭐 할래요?</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">4</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b10_dinner.webp\" alt=\"저녁\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저녁')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">저녁</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">jeonyeok</div><div class=\"vw-en\">dinner / evening</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u8_movie.webp\" alt=\"영화\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('영화')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">영화</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">yeonghwa</div><div class=\"vw-en\">movie</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u5_noraebang.webp\" alt=\"노래방\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('노래방')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">노래방</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">noraebang</div><div class=\"vw-en\">noraebang (karaoke room)</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b10_walk.webp\" alt=\"산책\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('산책')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">산책</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">sanchaek</div><div class=\"vw-en\">walk / stroll</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('오늘 저녁에 뭐 할래요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">오늘 저녁에 뭐 할래요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">What do you want to do tonight?</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('영화를 볼래요? 같이 봐요!')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">영화를 볼래요? 같이 봐요!</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Do you want to watch a movie? Let's watch together!</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저녁을 먹고 노래방에 갈까요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">저녁을 먹고 노래방에 갈까요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Shall we eat dinner and then go to the noraebang?</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('날씨가 좋아요. 같이 산책할까요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">날씨가 좋아요. 같이 산책할까요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">The weather is nice. Shall we take a walk together?</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🎬 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 저녁<b>을</b> 먹어요 (eat dinner), 영화<b>를</b> 봐요 (watch a movie), 노래방<b>에</b> 가요 (go to the noraebang), 산책<b>을</b> 해요 (take a walk). Ask 'want to ~?' with '할래요?'</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"pink\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🤝</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">친구와 같이<small>Together with friends · 몇 시에 만나요?</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">4</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a8_meet.webp\" alt=\"만나다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('만나다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">만나다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">mannada</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to meet</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a8_promise.webp\" alt=\"약속\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('약속')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">약속</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">yaksok</div><div class=\"vw-en\">promise / appointment</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b18_time.webp\" alt=\"시간\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('시간')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">시간</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">sigan</div><div class=\"vw-en\">time</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b10_together.webp\" alt=\"같이\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('같이')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">같이</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">gachi</div><div class=\"vw-en\">together</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('몇 시에 만날까요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">몇 시에 만날까요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">What time shall we meet?</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('오늘 약속이 있어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">오늘 약속이 있어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I have plans (an appointment) today.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('같이 시간을 보내요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">같이 시간을 보내요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Let's spend time together.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('친구와 같이 노래방에 가요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">친구와 같이 노래방에 가요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I go to the noraebang together with a friend.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🤝 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 만나다 → 만날까요? (shall we meet), 약속<b>이</b> 있어요 (have plans), 시간<b>이</b> 없어요 (have no time), 같이 = together.</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[8-1] Reading — 오늘 저녁에 뭐 할래요?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct answer.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">지우: 오늘 저녁에 뭐 할래요?</span> What is Jiwoo asking?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a8q1\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a8q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> \"I want dinner now.\"<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a8q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> What do you want to do tonight?<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a8q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> Where did you go last night?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a8q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> Let's make dinner.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a8q1\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The ending <b class=\"hl\">-을래요?</b> after a verb = <b class=\"hl\">\"do you want to ~?\"</b> (casual, to a friend). <b>뭐 할래요?</b> literally = \"what do you want to do?\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">\"where did you go\"</b> would be a past question (어디에 갔어요?), and the others add ideas (now / make) not in the sentence.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Rule: ask a friend \"do you want to ~?\" → <span class=\"pt-ko\">verb + 을래요? / ㄹ래요?</span></div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[8-2] Reading — 같이 영화를 볼래요?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct answer.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">하준: 같이 영화를 볼래요?</span> What does Hajun want to do?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a8q2\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a8q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> Watch a movie by himself<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a8q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> Watch a movie together<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a8q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> Eat dinner together<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a8q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> Go to the noraebang<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a8q2\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">같이</b> = <b class=\"hl\">\"together\"</b>. <b>영화를 볼래요</b> = \"want to watch a movie\", so <b>같이 영화를 볼래요?</b> = \"do you want to watch a movie together?\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">alone</b> is the opposite of 같이; the others name different activities (dinner / noraebang).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 같이 (together) invites your friend to join: 같이 + verb.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[8-3] Reading — -(으)ㄹ까요 suggestion</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct answer.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">서연: 노래방에 갈까요?</span> What does Seoyeon suggest?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a8q3\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a8q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> \"I want to go to the noraebang.\"<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a8q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> \"Shall we go to the noraebang?\"<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a8q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> \"I can't go to the noraebang.\"<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a8q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> \"We went to the noraebang.\"<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a8q3\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The ending <b class=\"hl\">-(으)ㄹ까요?</b> makes a <b class=\"hl\">soft suggestion</b> = \"shall we ~?\". <b>갈까요?</b> = \"shall we go?\" (가다 → 갈까요).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">want to</b> would be 갈래요, <b class=\"hl\">can't</b> = 못 가요, and <b class=\"hl\">went</b> = 갔어요. -ㄹ까요? is asking together.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Suggest a plan: verb + <span class=\"pt-ko\">ㄹ까요? / 을까요?</span></div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[8-4] Vocabulary — 같이</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct answer.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">저녁에 같이 먹을래요?</span> The word <b>같이</b> means</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a8q4\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a8q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> now<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a8q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> together<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a8q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> quickly<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a8q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> tonight<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a8q4\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">같이</b> = <b class=\"hl\">\"together\"</b> — used to include another person in the action: <b>같이 먹을래요?</b> = \"do you want to eat together?\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">now</b> = 지금, <b class=\"hl\">quickly</b> = 빨리, <b class=\"hl\">tonight</b> = 오늘 저녁. None fit \"together\".</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 같이 (together) is your key word for making plans with friends.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[8-5] Grammar — 뭐 할래요?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct answer.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">오늘 저녁에 뭐 (　)?</span> Choose the correct ending for \"what do you want to do?\"</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a8q5\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a8q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 하래요?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a8q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 할래요?<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a8q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 했을래요?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a8q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 할까요?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a8q5\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Verb <b class=\"hl\">하다</b> (do) → <b class=\"hl\">할래요?</b> (vowel + ㄹ래요). So <b>뭐 할래요?</b> = \"what do you want to do?\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">하래요?</b> is not a real form, <b class=\"hl\">했을래요?</b> mixes past, and <b class=\"hl\">할까요?</b> = \"shall I/we do?\" — a suggestion, not \"want to\".</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 하다 → <span class=\"pt-ko\">할래요?</span> \"want to do?\".</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[8-6] Grammar — 받침 · 먹을래요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct answer.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">배가 고파요. 밥을 (　).</span> \"I want to eat.\" Choose the correct form of 먹다.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a8q6\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a8q6',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 먹을까요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a8q6',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 먹을래요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a8q6',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 먹래요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a8q6',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 먹는래요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a8q6\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Verb <b class=\"hl\">먹다</b> (eat) ends in the consonant <b class=\"hl\">ㄱ</b>, so it takes <b class=\"hl\">-을래요</b>: <b>먹을래요</b> = \"I want to eat.\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">먹을까요?</b> = \"shall we eat?\" (suggestion), 먹래요 and 먹는래요 are wrong forms.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 받침 있으면 <span class=\"pt-ko\">-을래요</span>, 받침 없으면 <span class=\"pt-ko\">-ㄹ래요</span>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[8-7] Vocabulary — 노래방</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct answer.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">노래방</span> (noraebang) is a place where you</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a8q7\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a8q7',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> watch movies<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a8q7',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> sing songs<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a8q7',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> eat Korean food<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a8q7',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> exercise<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a8q7\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">노래방</b> = a <b class=\"hl\">karaoke room</b> where friends go to <b>sing (노래)</b>. After practice, idols love 노래방!</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">movies</b> are at the 영화관, Korean food at 식당, exercise at the 헬스장/운동.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 노래방에 가요 = \"go to the noraebang\". 같이 갈래요?</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[8-8] Vocabulary — 약속</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct answer.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">오늘 저녁에 약속이 있어요.</span> 약속 means</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a8q8\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a8q8',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> a phone<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a8q8',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> a gift<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a8q8',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> a promise / appointment (plans)<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a8q8',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> a walk<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a8q8\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">약속</b> = a <b class=\"hl\">promise / appointment</b> (plans). <b>약속이 있어요</b> = \"I have plans.\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">phone</b> = 전화/핸드폰, <b class=\"hl\">gift</b> = 선물, <b class=\"hl\">walk</b> = 산책.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 약속이 있어요 = busy (have plans); 약속이 없어요 = free (no plans).</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[8-9] Reading — 몇 시에 만날까요?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct answer.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">유나: 내일 몇 시에 만날까요?</span> What is Yuna asking?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a8q9\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a8q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> What time shall we meet tomorrow?<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a8q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> What did you do yesterday?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a8q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> Where is the meeting?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a8q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> When is your birthday?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a8q9\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">몇 시</b> = \"what time\", <b>만나다</b> (meet) → <b class=\"hl\">만날까요?</b> = \"shall we meet?\". So: \"What time shall we meet tomorrow?\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ The other options ask about yesterday, location, or birthday — not in the sentence.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Set a time with 만나다: 몇 시에 만날까요? 같이 시간을 정해요!</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[8-10] Vocabulary — 만나다</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct answer.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">주말에 친구를 만나요.</span> 친구를 만나다 means</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a8q10\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a8q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> to meet a friend<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a8q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> to call a friend<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a8q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> to miss a friend<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a8q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> to find a friend<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a8q10\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">만나다</b> = <b class=\"hl\">\"to meet\"</b>. <b>친구를 만나요</b> = \"I meet (my) friend.\" — perfect for planning an evening out!</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">call</b> = 전화하다, <b class=\"hl\">miss</b> = 보고 싶다, <b class=\"hl\">find</b> = 찾다.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 만나다 → 만날래요? (want to meet?) / 만날까요? (shall we meet?)</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "culture", "html": "<div class=\"culture\">\n    <span class=\"c-label\">🎤 K-POP TIP</span>\n    <h3>Plan Your Evening Like a K-POP Idol!</h3>\n    <p>After a long practice session, idols blow off steam by grabbing dinner, catching a movie, or hitting the noraebang together. Invite a friend with -을래요? and make it a group plan with 같이 and -(으)ㄹ까요? What is YOUR plan tonight?</p>\n    <div class=\"c-tip\">✍️ \"오늘 저녁에 같이 ○○할래요?\" — \"Do you want to ○○ together tonight?\"</div>\n  </div>"}]}, {"id": 9, "title": "I go to the mountains every weekend", "en": "주말마다 산에 가요", "theme": "weekend", "sections": [{"cls": "unit-flag", "html": "<div class=\"unit-flag\">UNIT 9 · WEEKEND</div>"}, {"cls": "sec-title", "html": "<div class=\"sec-title\"><div class=\"no\">9</div><div><h2>I go to the mountains every weekend</h2><div class=\"en\">주말마다 산에 가요 — Weekend · -마다, -(으)면서 &amp; -러 가다</div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "story", "html": "<div class=\"story\">\n    <img class=\"story-art\" src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n    <div class=\"story-body\">\n      <span class=\"story-tag\">💿 GLOWSIS STORY · NEW SEASON · WEEKEND</span>\n      <h3>주말마다 산에 가요 — &quot;I go to the mountains every weekend&quot;</h3>\n      <p>주말이 되면 다섯 멤버는 각자의 취미를 즐겨요. <b>지우</b>는 주말마다 <b>등산</b>을 하러 산에 가요. <b>유나</b>는 음악을 들으면서 <b>운동</b>을 해요. <b>하준</b>은 <b>사진</b>을 찍으러 공원에 가요. 그런데 이번 주말에는 다 같이 <b>낚시</b>하러 갈까요? 🎣</p>\n      <p class=\"story-en\">When the weekend comes the five members enjoy their own hobbies. <b>Jiwoo</b> goes hiking in the mountains every weekend. <b>Yuna</b> exercises while listening to music. <b>Hajun</b> goes to the park to take photos. But this weekend, should they all go fishing together? 🎣</p>\n      <span class=\"story-piece\">✨ NEW POINT · Say your every-weekend habits &amp; what you do while doing them!</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "goals", "html": "<div class=\"goals\">\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🗓️</span> Talk about what you do every weekend</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">✅</span> -마다 (every) &amp; -(으)면서 (while doing)</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🏔️</span> Hobbies &amp; weekend activity vocabulary</div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "dialog", "html": "<div class=\"dialog\">\n    <div class=\"d-head\">\n      <span class=\"d-title\">💬 Dialogue 9 — Weekend Hobbies</span>\n      <span class=\"d-scene\">🌿 A free weekend after rehearsal</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">지우</div><div class=\"ko\">주말마다 뭐 해요? 저는 주말마다 등산하러 산에 가요.</div><div class=\"gl\">What do you do every weekend? I go hiking in the mountains every weekend.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-05.webp\" alt=\"유나\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">유나</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 매일 음악을 들으면서 운동을 해요.</div><div class=\"gl\">I exercise while listening to music every day.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/m-05.webp\" alt=\"하준\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">하준</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 사진을 찍으러 공원에 가요. 같이 갈래요?</div><div class=\"gl\">I go to the park to take photos. Do you want to come?</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-02.webp\" alt=\"서연\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">서연</div><div class=\"ko\">좋아요! 이번 주말에 다 같이 낚시하러 가요! 🎣</div><div class=\"gl\">Great! This weekend let's all go fishing together! 🎣</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 1</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-마다 — &quot;every&quot; (time word)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">To say something happens <b>every</b> time period, attach <b>-마다</b> to the time word: <b>주말마다</b> = every weekend, <b>아침마다</b> = every morning. It turns one action into a habit.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">저는 주말마다 산에 가요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I go to the mountains every weekend. (주말 + 마다)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">유나는 아침마다 커피를 마셔요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Yuna drinks coffee every morning. (아침 + 마다)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">하준은 날마다 운동을 해요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Hajun exercises every day. (날 + 마다)</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 2</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-(으)면서 — &quot;while doing&quot;</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">To say two things happen <b>at the same time</b>, attach <b>-으면서</b> after a final consonant and <b>-면서</b> after a vowel: 듣다 → 들<b>으면서</b>, 하다 → 하<b>면서</b>. It means &quot;while doing…&quot;.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">음악을 들으면서 운동해요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I exercise while listening to music. (들다 → 들으면서)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">노래를 부르면서 걸어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I walk while singing. (부르다 → 부르면서)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">텔레비전을 보면서 밥을 먹어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I eat while watching TV. (보다 → 보면서)</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 3</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-러 가다 — &quot;go to do&quot;</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">To say you <b>go (somewhere) to do something</b>, change the verb to its <b>-러</b> form and add <b>가다</b>: 등산하다 → 등산하<b>러 가다</b> = &quot;go to hike&quot;, 사진을 찍다 → 사진을 찍<b>으러 가다</b> = &quot;go to take photos&quot;.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">저는 등산하러 산에 가요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I go to the mountain to hike. (등산하다 → 등산하러)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">친구를 만나러 공원에 가요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I go to the park to meet a friend. (만나다 → 만나러)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">물고기를 잡으러 바다에 가요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I go to the sea to catch fish. (잡다 → 잡으러)</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "teach", "html": "<div class=\"teach\">\n  <span class=\"t-label\">🧑‍🏫 Teacher's Deep-Dive · Breaking down \"저는 주말마다 산에 가요\"</span>\n  <div class=\"t-q\"><span class=\"t-ko\">저는 주말마다 산에 가요.</span> <span class=\"t-en\">= \"I go to the mountains every weekend.\"</span></div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-row t-head\">\n    <div class=\"t-why\">How do Korean idols say what they do again and again — like going hiking <b>every</b> weekend? The secret is a tiny word glued onto the time.</div>\n    <div class=\"t-deep\">\n      In English we say \"every weekend\" with the word <b>every</b> in front. Korean does it the other way — it sticks <b>마다</b> onto the time word: <b>주말</b> (weekend) + <b>마다</b> = <b>주말마다</b> (every weekend). Same idea for other habits. Today's sentence\n      <span class=\"pt-ko\">저는 주말마다 산에 가요</span> = \"I go to the mountains every weekend\" — a repeating weekend habit, not just one trip.\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-grid\">\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">저는</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">as for me <span class=\"t-sub\">(topic)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">저 = humble \"I\". Add <b>는</b> to introduce who you are talking about.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">주말마다</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">every weekend <span class=\"t-sub\">(주말 + 마다)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\"><b>주말</b> (weekend) + <b>마다</b> (every) = every weekend. The <b>마다</b> marks repetition — each and every time.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">산에</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">to the mountain <span class=\"t-sub\">(place + 에)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\"><b>산</b> (mountain) + <b>에</b> (to) = to the mountain. <b>에</b> points where you are going.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-eqcell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">가요</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">go <span class=\"t-sub\">(가다)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\"><b>가다</b> (to go) → <b>가요</b> (go, friendly polite). Put it with 마다 and you have a habit.</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-insight\">\n    <b class=\"t-i-ko\">마다 = \"every\"</b> — attach it to a time word to say something happens again and again. <b>주말마다 산에 가요</b> = \"I go to the mountains every weekend\", <b>아침마다 커피를 마셔요</b> = \"I drink coffee every morning\". It turns one action into a habit!\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-compare\">\n    <div class=\"t-c-a\"><b>주말마다 → every weekend (a habit)</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">저는 주말마다 산에 가요.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">\"I go to the mountains every weekend.\" — it happens over and over.</span></div>\n    <div class=\"t-c-b\"><b>주말에 → on the weekend (one time)</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">저는 주말에 영화를 봐요.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">\"I watch a movie on the weekend.\" — about this weekend, not a routine.</span></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-tip\">\n    💡 <b>Memory tip:</b> think of <b>마다</b> as the \"repeat button\". Say what you do EVERY week like an idol in practice: <span class=\"pt-ko\">저는 주말마다 등산을 해요!</span> (\"I go hiking every weekend!\"). To say what you do every single day, just use the word <span class=\"pt-ko\">매일</span>.\n  </div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "vocab-lab", "html": "<div class=\"vocab-lab\"><div class=\"vl-toolbar\"><span class=\"vl-hint\">카테고리를 눌러 그림과 함께 공부하세요</span><button class=\"vl-expand\" onclick=\"glowVocabAll()\">모두 펼치기</button></div><div class=\"vl-cat open\" data-tone=\"sky\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">⏰</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">주말과 시간<small>Time · every weekend & every day</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">2</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a9_weekend.webp\" alt=\"주말\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('주말')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">주말</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">jumal</div><div class=\"vw-en\">weekend</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a9_everyday.webp\" alt=\"매일\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('매일')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">매일</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">maeil</div><div class=\"vw-en\">every day</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저는 주말마다 산에 가요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">저는 주말마다 산에 가요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I go to the mountains every weekend.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저는 매일 운동을 해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">저는 매일 운동을 해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I exercise every day.</span></div></div></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat \" data-tone=\"lav\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🏔️</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">산과 공원<small>Mountains & parks · 어디에 가요?</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">2</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a6_mountain.webp\" alt=\"산\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('산')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">산</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">san</div><div class=\"vw-en\">mountain</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u8_park.webp\" alt=\"공원\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('공원')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">공원</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">gongwon</div><div class=\"vw-en\">park</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('산에서 공기가 좋아요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">산에서 공기가 좋아요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">The air is nice in the mountains.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('주말에 공원에 가요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">주말에 공원에 가요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I go to the park on the weekend.</span></div></div></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat \" data-tone=\"mint\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🏃</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">주말 활동<small>Weekend hobbies · 뭐를 해요?</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">4</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a9_hiking.webp\" alt=\"등산\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('등산')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">등산</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">deungsan</div><div class=\"vw-en\">hiking</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u5_exercise.webp\" alt=\"운동\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('운동')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">운동</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">undong</div><div class=\"vw-en\">exercise</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a9_fishing.webp\" alt=\"낚시\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('낚시')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">낚시</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">nakksi</div><div class=\"vw-en\">fishing</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a9_photo.webp\" alt=\"사진\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('사진')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">사진</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">sajin</div><div class=\"vw-en\">photo</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('등산하러 산에 가요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">등산하러 산에 가요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I go to the mountains to hike.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('음악을 들으면서 운동해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">음악을 들으면서 운동해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I exercise while listening to music.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('사진 찍으러 공원에 가요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">사진 찍으러 공원에 가요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I go to the park to take photos.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🏃 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 활동 이름 + <b>하러 가요</b> = \"go to do ○○\": <b>등산하러 가요</b>, <b>낚시하러 가요</b>. To say you do two things at once, use <b>-(으)면서</b>: <b>들으면서</b>.</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[9-1] Reading — 저는 주말마다 산에 가요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct answer.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">지우: 저는 주말마다 산에 가요.</span> What does Jiwoo say?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a9q1\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a9q1',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> I go to the mountains only on Sundays.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a9q1',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> I went to the mountains this weekend.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a9q1',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> I go to the mountains every weekend.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a9q1',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> I can't go to the mountains on weekends.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a9q1\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">마다</b> after a time word = <b class=\"hl\">\"every\"</b>. <b>주말마다</b> = 주말(weekend) + 마다 = <b class=\"hl\">every weekend</b>, so the sentence means \"I go to the mountains every weekend\".</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">only on Sundays</b> adds an idea (Sundays only) that isn't there; <b class=\"hl\">went</b> is past tense (갔어요), and <b class=\"hl\">can't</b> would need 못. None match 주말마다.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Rule: time word + <span class=\"pt-ko\">마다</span> = \"every ○○\". 주말마다, 아침마다…</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[9-2] Reading — fill in -마다</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct answer.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">저는 주말(　) 산에 가요.</span> = \"I go to the mountains every weekend.\"</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a9q2\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a9q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 동안 (during)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a9q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 마다 (every)<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a9q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 에서 (at/in)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a9q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 에 (to)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a9q2\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The sentence talks about a <b class=\"hl\">repeating habit</b> — every weekend — so the answer is <b class=\"hl\">마다</b>: <span class=\"pt-ko\">주말마다</span> = \"every weekend\".</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">동안</b> means \"during\", <b class=\"hl\">에서</b> is a place marker, and <b class=\"hl\">에</b> is \"to\" — none make the \"every\" meaning.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Fill \"every\" with <span class=\"pt-ko\">N + 마다</span>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[9-3] Reading — 음악을 들으면서 운동해요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct answer.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">지훈: 저는 음악을 들으면서 운동을 해요.</span> What does Jihoon mean?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a9q3\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a9q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> He exercises, then he listens to music.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a9q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> He listens to music while he exercises.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a9q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> He doesn't listen to music when he exercises.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a9q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> He exercises instead of listening to music.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a9q3\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The ending <b class=\"hl\">-(으)면서</b> means <b class=\"hl\">\"while doing\"</b>. <b>들으면서</b> = \"while listening\", so <span class=\"pt-ko\">음악을 들으면서 운동을 해요</span> = \"I exercise while listening to music\".</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">then</b> means one after the other, <b class=\"hl\">doesn't</b> is a negative, and <b class=\"hl\">instead of</b> changes the meaning — the two actions happen <b>at the same time</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <span class=\"pt-ko\">-(으)면서</span> = two actions at once: 듣다 → 들으면서.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[9-4] Reading — fill in -(으)면서</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct answer.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">서연은 노래를 부르(　) 등산을 해요.</span> = \"Seoyeon hikes while singing.\"</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a9q4\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a9q4',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 면서<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a9q4',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 러<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a9q4',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 니까<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a9q4',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 고서<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a9q4\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The verb <b class=\"hl\">부르다</b> (to sing) ends in a vowel, so it takes <b class=\"hl\">-면서</b> → <span class=\"pt-ko\">부르면서</span> = \"while singing\". The two actions happen at once.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">러</b> would be for \"go to do\" (-러 가다), <b class=\"hl\">니까</b> means \"because/so\", and <b class=\"hl\">고서</b> means \"and then\" — none mean \"while\".</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Vowel stem + <span class=\"pt-ko\">면서</span>: 부르다 → 부르면서.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[9-5] Listening — what he does every weekend</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Listen and choose the correct answer.</div>\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('저는 주말마다 낚시를 해요. 낚시는 정말 재미있어요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">What does the speaker do EVERY weekend?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a9q5\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a9q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 등산 (hiking)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a9q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 낚시 (fishing)<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a9q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 운동 (exercise)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a9q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 사진 찍기 (taking photos)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a9q5\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The audio says <span class=\"pt-ko\">주말마다 낚시를 해요</span> = \"I go fishing every weekend\". The word <b class=\"hl\">마다</b> tells us it is every weekend, and the activity is <b class=\"hl\">낚시 (fishing)</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ Hiking, exercise, and photos are not the activity the speaker does every weekend.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Listen for the activity noun + <span class=\"pt-ko\">-을/를 해요</span>: 낚시를 해요 = \"do fishing\".</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[9-6] Reading — 사진 찍으러 공원에 가요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct answer.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">유나: 저는 사진 찍으러 공원에 가요.</span> Why does Yuna go to the park?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a9q6\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a9q6',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> She goes to the park every day.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a9q6',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> She goes to the park to take pictures.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a9q6',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> She goes to the park to exercise.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a9q6',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> She went to the park last weekend.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a9q6\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The pattern <b class=\"hl\">-러 가다</b> = <b class=\"hl\">\"go (somewhere) in order to do\"</b>. <span class=\"pt-ko\">사진 찍으러 공원에 가요</span> = \"I go to the park to take photos\".</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">every day</b> needs 마다/매일, <b class=\"hl\">to exercise</b> would be 운동하러, and <b class=\"hl\">went</b> is past tense. The reason is taking pictures.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 verb stem + <span class=\"pt-ko\">-러 가다</span> = go to do ○○: 찍으러 가요, 운동하러 가요.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[9-7] Reading — choose the wrong sentence</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct answer.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Pick the sentence that has a mistake.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a9q7\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a9q7',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 저는 주말마다 산에 가요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a9q7',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 저는 매일마다 운동을 해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a9q7',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 저는 노래를 들으면서 청소를 해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a9q7',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 저는 등산하러 산에 가요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a9q7\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">매일</b> already means <b class=\"hl\">\"every day\"</b> on its own, so you do NOT add 마다. <span class=\"pt-ko\">매일마다</span> is a double \"every\" — it is wrong. Use just <span class=\"pt-ko\">매일 운동을 해요</span>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ The others are all correct: <b class=\"hl\">주말마다</b> (every weekend), <b class=\"hl\">들으면서</b> (while listening), and <b class=\"hl\">등산하러 가요</b> (go to hike).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 매일 = every day already — no extra 마다 needed.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[9-8] Listening — who goes hiking</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Listen and choose the correct answer.</div>\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('하준은 주말마다 등산을 해요. 유나는 주말마다 공원에서 운동을 해요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Listen to the audio. Who goes hiking every weekend?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a9q8\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a9q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 하준<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a9q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 유나<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a9q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 지우<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a9q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 서연<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a9q8\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The audio says <span class=\"pt-ko\">하준은 주말마다 등산을 해요</span> = \"Hajun goes hiking every weekend\" — the hiker is <b class=\"hl\">하준</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">유나</b> is named too, but she exercises (운동) in the park, not hikes. The other two are not mentioned.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 등산 = hiking. Listen for who is <span class=\"pt-ko\">주말마다 등산을 해요</span>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[9-9] Reading — best reply to 주말에 뭐 해요?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct answer.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">주말에 뭐 해요?</span> (What do you do on weekends?)</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a9q9\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a9q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 저는 공원에 갔어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a9q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 저는 주말마다 등산하러 산에 가요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a9q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 저는 지금 학교에 가요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a9q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 저는 내일 낚시를 할 거예요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a9q9\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The question asks about a <b class=\"hl\">weekend habit</b>, so the best answer uses <span class=\"pt-ko\">주말마다</span>: \"I go to the mountains to hike every weekend.\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">갔어요</b> is past, <b class=\"hl\">지금</b> (now) and <b class=\"hl\">내일</b> (tomorrow) answer a different time — only option 2 talks about the usual weekend.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Answer \"뭐 해요?\" (habit) with <span class=\"pt-ko\">주말마다 ○○해요</span> or <span class=\"pt-ko\">○○하러 가요</span>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[9-10] Listening — the idol weekend summary</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Listen and choose the correct answer.</div>\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('저는 주말마다 산에 가요. 산에서 노래를 부르면서 사진을 찍어요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">What does the speaker do every weekend?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a9q10\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a9q10',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> She goes to the park to take photos.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a9q10',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> She sings and takes photos while she hikes in the mountains.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a9q10',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> She goes fishing every weekend.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a9q10',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> She only takes photos at home.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a9q10\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The speaker says <span class=\"pt-ko\">주말마다 산에 가요</span> (I go to the mountains every weekend) and <span class=\"pt-ko\">노래를 부르면서 사진을 찍어요</span> (I take photos while singing). Best summary: <b class=\"hl\">she sings and takes photos while she hikes in the mountains</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ It is the <b class=\"hl\">mountains</b>, not the park; it is <b class=\"hl\">hiking + photos</b>, not fishing; and the action is outdoors, not at home.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 A great weekend mix — <span class=\"pt-ko\">-마다</span> for the habit, <span class=\"pt-ko\">-(으)면서</span> for doing two things at once!</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "culture", "html": "<div class=\"culture\">\n    <span class=\"c-label\">🎤 K-POP TIP</span>\n    <h3>Weekends Like a K-POP Idol!</h3>\n    <p>Between comebacks, idols recharge with real hobbies — hiking mountains, taking photos, fishing, or working out while listening to music. They turn each weekend into a small habit. Use -마다 to say what you do EVERY weekend, -(으)면서 for doing two things at once, and -러 가다 when you GO somewhere to do it!</p>\n    <div class=\"c-tip\">✍️ &quot;저는 주말마다 노래를 들으면서 산책하러 공원에 가요.&quot; — &quot;(Every weekend I go to the park for a walk while listening to music.)&quot;</div>\n  </div>"}]}, {"id": 10, "title": "Be quiet after 10pm", "en": "밤 10시 이후로는 조용히 할 것", "theme": "rules", "sections": [{"cls": "unit-flag", "html": "<div class=\"unit-flag\">UNIT 10 · DORM RULES</div>"}, {"cls": "sec-title", "html": "<div class=\"sec-title\"><div class=\"no\">10</div><div><h2>Be quiet after 10pm</h2><div class=\"en\">밤 10시 이후로는 조용히 할 것 — Dorm rules · -(으)ㄹ 거예요 &amp; -아/어야 돼요</div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "story", "html": "<div class=\"story\">\n    <img class=\"story-art\" src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n    <div class=\"story-body\">\n      <span class=\"story-tag\">💿 GLOWSIS STORY · DORM LIFE · RULES</span>\n      <h3>우리 숙소의 규칙 — \"조용히 해야 돼요!\"</h3>\n      <p>콘서트가 끝나고 멤버들은 같은 <b>숙소</b>에서 살아요. <b>지우</b>가 벽에 <b>규칙</b>을 붙였어요. <b>밤 10시 이후로는 조용히 할 것!</b> 옆방에 <b>이웃</b>이 있으니까 밤에는 꼭 조용히 해야 돼요. 그런데 <b>하준</b>이 시끄럽게 노래해요... 😂</p>\n      <p class=\"story-en\">After the concert the members all live in the same <b>dorm</b>. <b>Jiwoo</b> taped up the <b>rules</b>: \"Be quiet after 10pm!\" Because there are <b>neighbors</b> next door, they must be quiet at night. But <b>Hajun</b> is singing loudly… 😂</p>\n      <span class=\"story-piece\">✨ NEW POINT · Talk about dorm rules, future plans & what you must do!</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "goals", "html": "<div class=\"goals\">\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🌓</span> Say future plans with -(으)ㄹ 거예요</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🔊</span> 조용히 vs 시끄럽게 (quietly vs noisily)</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🏠</span> Say rules & obligations with -아/어야 돼요</div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "dialog", "html": "<div class=\"dialog\">\n    <div class=\"d-head\">\n      <span class=\"d-title\">💬 Dialogue 10 — Dorm Rules</span>\n      <span class=\"d-scene\">🏠 Shared dorm, night time</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">지우</div><div class=\"ko\">여러분, 우리 숙소의 규칙이에요. 밤 10시 이후로는 조용히 해야 돼요.</div><div class=\"gl\">Everyone, these are our dorm rules. After 10pm you must be quiet.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/m-05.webp\" alt=\"하준\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">하준</div><div class=\"ko\">네, 알겠어요. 저는 10시부터 노래를 조용히 연습할 거예요.</div><div class=\"gl\">Yes, got it. From 10 I will practice singing quietly.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-05.webp\" alt=\"유나\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">유나</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 헤드폰을 쓸 거예요. 이웃이 시끄러워하면 안 돼요!</div><div class=\"gl\">I will wear headphones. The neighbors must not be disturbed!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-02.webp\" alt=\"서연\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">서연</div><div class=\"ko\">그래요. 밤에는 조용히 해야 돼요. 예의가 중요해요!</div><div class=\"gl\">Right. At night we must be quiet. Manners matter!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/m-01.webp\" alt=\"지훈\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">지훈</div><div class=\"ko\">주의! 벽을 치면 안 돼요. 우리 모두 조용히 할 거예요. 👍</div><div class=\"gl\">Careful! No hitting the walls. We'll all be quiet. 👍</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 1</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-(으)ㄹ 거예요 — Future plan & intention (I will / am going to)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">To say what you <b>plan</b> or <b>intend</b> to do, add <b>-ㄹ 거예요</b> after a vowel and <b>-을 거예요</b> after a final consonant. So 하다(do) → <b>할 거예요</b> = \"I will do\". It's the most common way to say your plan for tonight or tomorrow.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">저는 밤 10시부터 조용히 할 거예요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I will be quiet from 10pm. (하다 → 할 거예요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">유나는 일찍 잘 거예요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Yuna will sleep early. (자다 → 잘 거예요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">저는 노래를 조용히 연습할 거예요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I will practice singing quietly. (연습하다 → 연습할 거예요)</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 2</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">조용히 &amp; 시끄럽게 — Quietly vs noisily (adverbs)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">From the adjectives <b>조용하다</b>(quiet) and <b>시끄럽다</b>(noisy) we make the adverbs <b>조용히</b>(quietly) and <b>시끄럽게</b>(noisily). Put them right before the verb to describe HOW you do it — so <b>조용히 해요</b> = \"do it quietly, be quiet\".</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">밤에는 조용히 해요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Be quiet at night.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">숙소에서 시끄럽게 하면 안 돼요.</span><span class=\"gl\">You mustn't be noisy in the dorm.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">하준은 노래를 크고 시끄럽게 불러요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Hajun sings loudly and noisily.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 3</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-아/어야 돼요 — Must / have to (obligation)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">To say you <b>must</b> do something, add <b>-아야 돼요</b> after stems with ㅏ/ㅗ and <b>-어야 돼요</b> after others; 하다 becomes <b>해야 돼요</b>. This is how you talk about rules and duties — perfect for a dorm or concert hall!</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">숙소에서는 조용히 해야 돼요.</span><span class=\"gl\">You must be quiet in the dorm. (하다 → 해야 돼요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">규칙을 지켜야 돼요.</span><span class=\"gl\">You must follow the rules. (지키다 → 지켜야 돼요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">이웃을 생각해야 돼요.</span><span class=\"gl\">You must think of your neighbors.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "teach", "html": "<div class=\"teach\">\n  <span class=\"t-label\">🧑🏻‍🏫 Teacher's Deep-Dive · Breaking down \"밤 10시 이후로는 조용히 해야 돼요\"</span>\n  <div class=\"t-q\"><span class=\"t-ko\">밤 10시 이후로는 조용히 해야 돼요.</span> <span class=\"t-en\">= \"After 10pm, you must be quiet.\"</span></div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-row t-head\">\n    <div class=\"t-why\">Dorm rules aren't just for school — K-POP idols share a <b>숙소</b> (dorm) too! How do they say a rule like \"be quiet after 10pm\"?</div>\n    <div class=\"t-deep\">\n      A rule uses <b>-아/어야 돼요</b>, the \"must\" ending, plus the adverb <b>조용히</b> (quietly). To flip it into a personal PLAN, idols switch the ending to\n      <span class=\"pt-ko\">-(으)ㄹ 거예요</span>. So the dorm leader says <b>해야 돼요</b> (you MUST), and each member answers <b>할 거예요</b> (I WILL). Two tiny endings turn a rule into a promise!\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-grid\">\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">밤 10시 <b>이후로는</b></div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">after 10pm <span class=\"t-sub\">(time topic)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">밤 = night, 10시 = 10 o'clock. 이후로는 = \"from after …\" — it sets the rule's starting time.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">조용히</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">quietly <span class=\"t-sub\">(adverb)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">From <b>조용하다</b>(quiet). Adverbs go right before the verb and describe HOW you do it.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-eqcell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">해야 돼요</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">must do <span class=\"t-sub\">(-아/어야 돼요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\"><b>하다</b> → <b>해야 돼요</b> = \"must do\". This is the obligation ending for rules.</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-insight\">\n    <b class=\"t-i-ko\">Rules vs plans — two endings that pair perfectly.</b> A <b>rule</b> for everyone uses <span class=\"pt-ko\">-아/어야 돼요</span>\n    (조용히 해야 돼요 = must be quiet). A <b>personal plan</b> uses <span class=\"pt-ko\">-(으)ㄹ 거예요</span> (조용히 할 거예요 = I will be quiet).\n    The leader states the rule; each member promises a plan. Together they keep the dorm peaceful!\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-compare\">\n    <div class=\"t-c-a\"><b>Rule / must → -아/어야 돼요</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">밤에는 조용히 해야 돼요.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">\"You must be quiet at night.\" — a rule for everyone.</span></div>\n    <div class=\"t-c-b\"><b>Plan / will → -(으)ㄹ 거예요</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">저는 밤에는 조용히 할 거예요.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">\"I will be quiet at night.\" — my own intention.</span></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-tip\">\n    💡 <b>Memory tip:</b> <span class=\"pt-ko\">해야 돼요</span> = \"you HAVE to\" (a duty), <span class=\"pt-ko\">할 거예요</span> = \"I WILL\" (a plan).\n    Next time you hear a dorm rule, reply like an idol: <span class=\"pt-ko\">네, 알겠어요. 저는 조용히 할 거예요!</span> (\"Yes, got it — I'll be quiet!\")\n  </div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "vocab-lab", "html": "<div class=\"vocab-lab\"><div class=\"vl-toolbar\"><span class=\"vl-hint\">카테고리를 눌러 그림과 함께 공부하세요</span><button class=\"vl-expand\" onclick=\"glowVocabAll()\">모두 펼치기</button></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"mint\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🌙</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">밤의 소리<small>Night sounds · 조용히 &amp; 시끄럽게</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">2</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a10_quiet.webp\" alt=\"조용하다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('조용하다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">조용하다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">joyonghada</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to be quiet</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a10_noisy.webp\" alt=\"시끄럽다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('시끄럽다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">시끄럽다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">kkeureopda</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to be noisy</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('밤에는 조용히 해야 돼요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">밤에는 조용히 해야 돼요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">At night we must be quiet.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('하준이 너무 시끄러워요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">하준이 너무 시끄러워요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Hajun is too noisy.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('조용히 말해 주세요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">조용히 말해 주세요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Please speak quietly.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🌙 <b>반대말:</b> 조용하<b>다</b>(quiet) ↔ 시끄럽<b>다</b>(noisy). Adverbs: 조용<b>히</b> = quietly, 시끄럽<b>게</b> = noisily.</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"sky\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🏠</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">숙소 생활<small>Dorm life · 규칙 &amp; 이웃</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">4</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a10_dorm.webp\" alt=\"숙소\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('숙소')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">숙소</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">sukso</div><div class=\"vw-en\">dorm / shared lodging</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a10_rule.webp\" alt=\"규칙\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('규칙')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">규칙</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">gyuchik</div><div class=\"vw-en\">rule</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a10_neighbor.webp\" alt=\"이웃\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('이웃')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">이웃</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">iut</div><div class=\"vw-en\">neighbor</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a10_night.webp\" alt=\"밤\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('밤')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">밤</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">bam</div><div class=\"vw-en\">night</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('우리는 같은 숙소에서 살아요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">우리는 같은 숙소에서 살아요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">We live in the same dorm.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('숙소에는 규칙이 있어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">숙소에는 규칙이 있어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">The dorm has rules.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('밤 10시 이후로는 조용히 해야 돼요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">밤 10시 이후로는 조용히 해야 돼요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">After 10pm you must be quiet.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('이웃을 위해서 조용히 해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">이웃을 위해서 조용히 해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">We stay quiet for our neighbors.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🏠 <b>숙소 = dorm</b> where idols live together. To keep it peaceful we follow the <b>규칙</b> and think of our <b>이웃</b> (neighbors).</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"lav\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🙏</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">예의와 주의<small>Manners &amp; care · 팬과 이웃을 위해</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">2</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a10_manners.webp\" alt=\"예의\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('예의')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">예의</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">yeui</div><div class=\"vw-en\">manners / politeness</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/2a10_attention.webp\" alt=\"주의\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('주의')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">주의</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">jueui</div><div class=\"vw-en\">care / caution</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('아이돌은 팬에게 예의가 있어야 돼요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">아이돌은 팬에게 예의가 있어야 돼요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">An idol must have manners toward fans.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('밤에는 소리에 주의해야 돼요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">밤에는 소리에 주의해야 돼요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">At night you must be careful about noise.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🙏 <b>예의</b> = good manners, <b>주의</b> = being careful. Idols stay kind (예의) and careful (주의) so fans and neighbors feel respected.</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[10-1] Reading — -(으)ㄹ 거예요 (future plan)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose what Jiwoo plans to do.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">지우: 저는 밤 10시 이후로는 조용히 할 거예요.</span> What does Jiwoo plan to do?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a10q1\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a10q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> I was quiet last night.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a10q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> I will be quiet after 10pm.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a10q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> You must be quiet now.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a10q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> Please be quiet.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a10q1\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏻‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The ending <b class=\"hl\">-(으)ㄹ 거예요</b> = <b class=\"hl\">\"will / am going to\"</b> (a plan or intention). <b>하다</b>(do) → <b>할 거예요</b> = \"will do\". So <span class=\"pt-ko\">조용히 할 거예요</span> = \"I will be quiet\".</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓠ <b class=\"hl\">\"must\"</b> (해야 돼요) and past (했어요) are different meanings; \"please\" would be a request.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Rule: plan &amp; intention → <span class=\"pt-ko\">verb + -(으)ㄹ 거예요</span>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[10-2] Reading — -아/어야 돼요 (must)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct meaning.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">하준: 숙소에서는 밤에 조용히 해야 돼요.</span> What does this mean?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a10q2\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a10q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> I must be quiet at night in the dorm.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a10q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> I can be quiet at night.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a10q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> I will be quiet at night.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a10q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> I was quiet last night.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a10q2\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏻‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">-아/어야 돼요</b> = <b class=\"hl\">\"must / have to\"</b>. <b>하다</b>(do) → <b>해야 돼요</b> = \"have to do\", so <span class=\"pt-ko\">조용히 해야 돼요</span> = \"must be quiet\".</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓠ \"can\" uses <span class=\"pt-ko\">ㄹ 수 있어요</span>, \"will\" uses <span class=\"pt-ko\">ㄹ 거예요</span>, and the past uses 했어요.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Rule: duty / obligation → <span class=\"pt-ko\">verb stem + 아야/어야 돼요</span>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[10-3] Reading — 조용히 vs 시끄럽게</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the adverb that means \"quietly, without noise\".</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Which word means <b class=\"hl\">quietly</b>?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a10q3\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a10q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 조용히<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a10q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 시끄럽게<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a10q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 빨리<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a10q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 천천히<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a10q3\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏻‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The adverb <b class=\"hl\">조용히</b> comes from <span class=\"pt-ko\">조용하다</span>(to be quiet). At night we say <span class=\"pt-ko\">조용히 해요</span> = \"be quiet / do it quietly\".</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓠ <b class=\"hl\">시끄럽게</b> = noisily (the opposite), 빨리 = fast, 천천히 = slowly.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <span class=\"pt-ko\">조용하다</span> → <span class=\"pt-ko\">조용히</span> (quietly); <span class=\"pt-ko\">시끄럽다</span> → <span class=\"pt-ko\">시끄럽게</span> (noisily).</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[10-4] Reading — 이웃 (neighbors)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the meaning of <b class=\"hl\">이웃</b>.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">\"우리 숙소 옆에 사는 사람들, 이웃이 있어요. 그래서 밤에는 조용히 해요.\" What is <span class=\"pt-ko\">이웃</span>?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a10q4\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a10q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> The managers<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a10q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> The fans<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a10q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> The neighbors<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a10q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> The members<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a10q4\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏻‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">In the passage <span class=\"pt-ko\">숙소 옆에 사는 사람들</span> = \"the people living next to the dorm\" = <b class=\"hl\">이웃</b> (neighbors).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓠ 매니저 = manager, 팬 = fan, 멤버 = member — none means \"next-door people\".</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Because <span class=\"pt-ko\">이웃</span> live nearby, idols stay <span class=\"pt-ko\">조용히</span> at night.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[10-5] Reading — 조용하다 / 시끄럽다</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and pick the right word for the dorm.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">하준이 밤에 노래를 크게 불러요. 그래서 숙소는 (　).</span></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a10q5\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a10q5',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 조용해요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a10q5',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 한가해요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a10q5',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 추워요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a10q5',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 시끄러워요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a10q5\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏻‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">하준 sings <b class=\"hl\">크게</b> (loudly) at night, so the dorm becomes <b class=\"hl\">시끄러워요</b> (noisy).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓠ <b class=\"hl\">조용해요</b> = it is quiet (the opposite); 한가해요 = free/not busy; 추워요 = cold.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <span class=\"pt-ko\">시끄럽다</span> → 시끄러워요 (it's noisy); <span class=\"pt-ko\">조용하다</span> → 조용해요 (it's quiet).</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[10-6] Reading — 규칙을 지켜야 돼요 (must follow rules)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the phrase that fits the rule.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">숙소에는 규칙이 있어요. 우리는 규칙을 (　).</span></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a10q6\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a10q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 지켜야 돼요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a10q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 지킬 거예요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a10q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 안 지켜요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a10q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 지킬 수 있어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a10q6\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏻‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">A rule means you <b class=\"hl\">have to</b> follow it: <span class=\"pt-ko\">규칙을 지켜야 돼요</span> = \"we must follow the rules\". The verb <span class=\"pt-ko\">지키다</span> = to follow / keep.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓠ <b class=\"hl\">지킬 거예요</b> (will), 안 지켜요 (don't), and 지킬 수 있어요 (can) are plans, denials, or abilities — not an obligation.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 \"must\" after <span class=\"pt-ko\">지키다</span>: 지켜야 돼요.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[10-7] Reading — 예의 (manners)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the meaning of <b class=\"hl\">예의</b>.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">\"아이돌은 항상 팬과 이웃에게 예의가 있어야 돼요.\" What is <span class=\"pt-ko\">예의</span>?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a10q7\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a10q7',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> Price<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a10q7',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> Manners / politeness<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a10q7',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> Noise<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a10q7',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> A song<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a10q7\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏻‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">예의가 있어야 돼요</span> = \"must have good manners / be polite\". Idols must show <b class=\"hl\">예의</b> (manners) to fans and neighbors.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓠ 값 = price, 소리 = sound/noise, 노래 = song — these do not fit being kind to people.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <span class=\"pt-ko\">예의</span> (manners) + <span class=\"pt-ko\">주의</span> (care) = being a considerate person.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[10-8] Listening — 밤에 조용히 해야 돼요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose what must happen after 10pm.</div>\n  <button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('밤 10시 이후로는 조용히 해야 돼요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">What must the members do after 10pm?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a10q8\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a10q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> Be quiet<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a10q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> Sing loudly<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a10q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> Eat a snack<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a10q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> Dance all night<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a10q8\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏻‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The audio says <span class=\"pt-ko\">밤 10시 이후로는 조용히 해야 돼요</span> = \"after 10pm you must be quiet\". The key word is <b class=\"hl\">해야 돼요</b> (must do).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓠ singing loudly, snacking, and dancing all night would make the neighbors <b class=\"hl\">시끄러워</b> — exactly what the rule stops.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Listen for <span class=\"pt-ko\">조용히 해야 돼요</span> — that's the rule to catch.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[10-9] Listening — 지훈의 계획 (Jihoon's plan)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose what Jihoon will do at night.</div>\n  <button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('이웃을 위해서 저는 밤에는 조용히 연습할 거예요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">What will Jihoon do at night for the neighbors?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a10q9\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a10q9',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> Sing loudly<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a10q9',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> Eat a snack<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a10q9',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> Watch TV<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a10q9',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> Practice quietly<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a10q9\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏻‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The audio says <span class=\"pt-ko\">저는 밤에는 조용히 연습할 거예요</span> = \"I will practice quietly at night\". <b class=\"hl\">연습할 거예요</b> uses the future plan ending -(으)ㄹ 거예요.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓠ Singing loudly, snacking, or watching TV would make noise — Jihoon stays <b class=\"hl\">조용히</b> for the neighbors.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <span class=\"pt-ko\">연습하다</span>(practice) → <span class=\"pt-ko\">연습할 거예요</span> (will practice).</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[10-10] Listening — 숙소 규칙 요약 (summary)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose the best summary of the dorm rules.</div>\n  <button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('우리 숙소는 조용해야 돼요. 밤 10시 이후로는 조용히 하고, 이웃을 위해서 주의할 거예요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Which is the best summary of what you heard?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"2a10q10\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a10q10',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> We can dance all night.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a10q10',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> We should be as loud as we want.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a10q10',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> Be quiet after 10pm and care about our neighbors.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('2a10q10',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> We never need to practice.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-2a10q10\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏻‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The clip brings together the whole lesson: <span class=\"pt-ko\">밤 10시 이후로는 조용히 하고, 이웃을 위해서 주의할 거예요</span>. Being quiet after 10 and caring about neighbors is the rule.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓠ Dancing all night, being loud, and never practicing all contradict the dorm <b class=\"hl\">규칙</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Key pattern: <span class=\"pt-ko\">조용히 하다</span> (be quiet) + <span class=\"pt-ko\">주의하다</span> (be careful) = considerate dorm life.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "culture", "html": "<div class=\"culture\">\n    <span class=\"c-label\">🎤 K-POP TIP</span>\n    <h3>Real Dorm Rules — Idols Keep It Quiet!</h3>\n    <p>K-POP groups really do live together in a <b>숙소</b>, and <b>조용히 하기</b> (being quiet) is one of the first rules! After a late practice they must <b>조용히 해야 돼요</b> so their <b>이웃</b> can rest. And at concerts, fans are asked to <b>주의</b> and show <b>예의</b> — no pushing, no screaming between songs. A considerate fan respects the rules and the artists around them.</p>\n    <div class=\"c-tip\">🙋 Try it: after a concert, an idol waves and says \"<b>오늘 밤에는 조용히 쉴 거예요!</b>\" — \"Tonight I'll rest quietly!\" Answer with a plan of your own using -(으)ㄹ 거예요.</div>\n  </div>"}]}];
